ATCCardsData("EN03",[["v5ljkr","Health: Every summer I get ______ from the chlorine in the pool: my eyes turn red, itchy and sticky. (starts with \"pin\")","pinkeye (conjuntivitis): eye infection that makes the eye red and sore; medical word \"conjunctivitis\". Not: hoarse (rough voice), dizzy (head spinning), rash (red spots on the skin)."],["1jla1ql","Health: After shouting at the match all afternoon, I was so ______ that I could barely speak. (starts with \"ho\")","hoarse (ronco, afónico): with a rough, weak voice. Not: husky (deep voice, often attractive), sore (painful: a sore throat), dumb (unable to speak, offensive today)."],["10rmmvb","Health: I stood up too quickly and felt ______, as if the room was spinning. (starts with \"di\")","dizzy (mareado): feeling that everything is turning and you may fall. Not: sick (about to vomit), faint (about to lose consciousness), seasick (on a boat)."],["rf9r2","Health: The X-rays showed the bone was badly broken, and ______ was needed to fix it with metal pins. (starts with \"su\")","surgery (cirugía): treatment by cutting the body open; uncountable here (\"need surgery\"). Not: operation (countable: \"an operation\"), remedy (home cure), cure (something that ends a disease)."],["1dbru9r","Health: She is recovering after a five-hour heart ______ on Monday. (starts with \"op\")","operation (operación): one act of surgery; countable (\"an operation\", \"two operations\"). Not: surgery (uncountable in \"have surgery\"), intervention (formal, wider), treatment (any medical care)."],["1cob7oj","Health: After three days of observation, the patient was ______ from hospital and told to rest at home. (starts with \"dis\")","discharged (dado de alta): officially allowed to leave hospital. Not: admitted (taken in), transferred (moved to another hospital), released (prisoners, news, films)."],["5pq6h0","Health: She was ______ to hospital with chest pains late last night. (starts with \"ad\")","admitted (ingresada): taken into hospital as a patient. Not: discharged (sent home), entered (not used for patients), interned (held as a prisoner)."],["z0b91e","Health: He broke his leg skiing and has to wear a ______ for six weeks. (starts with \"ca\")","cast (escayola): hard cover that holds a broken bone still; BrE also \"plaster cast\". Not: bandage (soft strip of cloth), sling (cloth that holds up an arm), splint (straight piece of wood or metal tied to a limb)."],["12bn9wa","Health: Until his ankle heals he has to walk on ______. (starts with \"cr\")","crutches (muletas): sticks that fit under the arms to help you walk. Not: walking stick (one stick; AmE cane), wheelchair, stretcher (frame for carrying a patient lying down)."],["lwjjda","Health: She had her arm in a ______ for a month after dislocating her shoulder. (starts with \"sl\")","sling (cabestrillo): piece of cloth tied round the neck to hold up an injured arm. Not: cast (hard cover), bandage (strip wound round), brace (support for the back, knee or teeth)."],["zaykq2","Health: The cut on his forehead was so deep that he needed six ______. (starts with \"st\")","stitches (puntos de sutura): short threads that close a wound. Not: plasters (small sticky strips; AmE Band-Aids), bandages, staples (metal clips)."],["eq52xa","Health: It's only a small cut; put a ______ on it so it doesn't get dirty. (starts with \"pl\")","plaster (tirita): small sticky strip for a cut; AmE Band-Aid. Not: cast (for a broken bone), bandage (long strip of cloth), stitch (for a deep wound)."],["2alitj","Health: You can't buy these antibiotics over the counter; you need a ______ from your doctor. (starts with \"pr\")","prescription (receta médica): doctor's written order for a medicine. Not: recipe (cooking instructions; false friend \"receta\"), receipt (proof of payment), description."],["iww1jd","Health: The pills cured the infection, but the ______ effects included headaches and nausea. (starts with \"si\")","side (effects) (efectos secundarios): unwanted effects of a medicine. Not: secondary effects (not the fixed phrase), after-effects (lasting effects after an illness or event), collateral."],["11atw6u","Health: I've got a ______ nose and I can't smell anything. (starts with \"bl\")","blocked (taponada): full of mucus so air cannot pass; AmE \"stuffy\". Not: runny (liquid comes out), closed, stuck."],["5dn8vj","Health: I ______ my ankle playing basketball, and now it's swollen. (starts with \"tw\")","twisted (me torcí): turned a joint too far and hurt it; also \"sprained\". Not: broke (a bone), bent (curved), dislocated (bone out of its joint)."],["5ra4l4","Health: After weeks of training without rest, the runner ______ a muscle in his thigh. (starts with \"pu\")","pulled (se dio un tirón): stretched and injured a muscle. Not: stretched (on purpose, safe), twisted (a joint), tore (worse: a torn muscle)."],["1qoivn2","Health: The child has a ______ of 39 degrees, so keep her in bed. (starts with \"te\")","temperature (fiebre): \"have a temperature\" = have a fever (BrE everyday phrase). Not: heat (of the weather or an oven), warmth (pleasant heat), fever (same meaning, but starts with \"f\")."],["1ybh4pm","Health: Wash your hands often: flu is highly ______ and spreads quickly in offices. (starts with \"con\")","contagious (contagioso): passing easily from person to person. Not: infectious (similar, starts with \"in\"), contaminated (made dirty or poisonous), contiguous (next to each other)."],["3k1uql","Health: The baby has a red, itchy ______ all over her chest. (starts with \"ra\")","rash (sarpullido, erupción): area of red spots on the skin. Not: blister (bubble of liquid under the skin), bruise (dark mark from a blow), spot (a single pimple)."],["f2tg6p","Health: I banged my leg on the table, and now I have a huge purple ______. (starts with \"br\")","bruise (moratón): dark mark on the skin after a blow. Not: rash (red spots), scar (mark left by a healed wound), blister (bubble from rubbing)."],["j79lih","Health: These new shoes have given me a ______ on my heel. (starts with \"bl\")","blister (ampolla): small bubble of liquid under the skin from rubbing or a burn. Not: bruise (from a blow), callus (hard skin), wound."],["qp7ajr","Health: The operation left a long ______ across his stomach. (starts with \"sc\")","scar (cicatriz): mark left on the skin after a wound heals. Not: scratch (light cut from nails or thorns), stitch (thread), wound (the injury itself)."],["170amzu","Health: I've had a ______ throat since Monday and it hurts to swallow. (starts with \"so\")","sore (dolorida): painful and red; \"a sore throat\" (dolor de garganta). Not: hoarse (rough voice, not pain), aching (dull pain in muscles or head), itchy."],["1roo2po","Health: The ______ arrived within minutes and treated him in the ambulance. (starts with \"pa\")","paramedics (técnicos de emergencias): trained ambulance staff who give emergency treatment. Not: nurses (in hospital), surgeons (operate), porters (move patients in hospital)."],["7ltsuz","Health: My son's ______ says his cough is nothing to worry about; she sees only children. (starts with \"pae\")","paediatrician (pediatra): doctor for children; AmE pediatrician. Not: gynaecologist (women's reproductive health), obstetrician (pregnancy and birth), physician (any doctor)."],["xm0z7x","Health: In Britain, your first stop for a non-urgent problem is the local ______, also called a GP. (two words, starts with \"gen\")","general practitioner (médico de cabecera): family doctor; short form GP. Not: physician (formal, any doctor), specialist (consultant in one field), surgeon."],["16x8tvf","Health: As a ______, she delivers babies and cares for mothers before and after the birth, although she is not a doctor. (starts with \"mi\")","midwife (matrona, comadrona): trained person, not a doctor, who helps women give birth. Not: nurse (general care), gynaecologist and obstetrician (doctors), nanny (looks after children)."],["1vguv0s","Health: The ______ who operated on my knee says I'll be running again in three months. (starts with \"su\")","surgeon (cirujano): doctor who performs operations. Not: physician (treats with medicines, does not operate), physiotherapist (exercise and massage), surgery (the treatment; BrE also a doctor's office)."],["vf21ht","Health: After the operation, a ______ gave me exercises and massage to get my knee moving again. (starts with \"phy\")","physiotherapist (fisioterapeuta): treats injuries with exercise and massage; AmE physical therapist. Not: physician (doctor), physicist (scientist of physics), chiropractor (adjusts the spine)."],["12psccz","Health: She chose not to specialise in surgery and works as a ______, treating patients in a clinic with diagnosis and medicines. (starts with \"phy\")","physician (médico): formal and AmE word for a doctor who treats with medicines rather than operations. Not: physicist (scientist of physics), physiotherapist (exercise and massage), surgeon (operates)."],["drlgqy","Health: The ______ at the pharmacy explained how often to take the tablets. (starts with \"pha\")","pharmacist (farmacéutico): person qualified to prepare and sell medicines; BrE also chemist. Not: pharmacy (the shop), druggist (old AmE), physician (doctor)."],["1m34d13","Health: The patient slipped into a ______ after the accident and didn't wake up for three weeks. (starts with \"co\")","coma (coma): long state of deep unconsciousness. Not: faint (short loss of consciousness), trance, sleep."],["l2ctl2","Health: It was so hot in the queue that an old man ______ and fell to the ground. (starts with \"fa\")","fainted (se desmayó): lost consciousness for a short time; informal \"passed out\". Not: collapsed (fell down suddenly, cause open), fell asleep, passed away (died)."],["1t3uy8f","Health: Sadly, my grandfather ______ away peacefully in his sleep last night. (starts with \"pa\")","passed (away) (falleció): polite way to say died. Not: passed out (fainted), passed by (went past), passed over (ignored for a promotion)."],["1cuhifl","Health: The new vaccine gives ______ against all known strains of the virus. (starts with \"im\")","immunity (inmunidad): protection against a disease. Not: impunity (escaping punishment), immunisation (the act of vaccinating), resistance (of germs to drugs)."],["1kv58eg","Health: To stop the disease spreading, travellers from the area were kept in ______ for fourteen days. (starts with \"qu\")","quarantine (cuarentena): period of isolation to stop a disease spreading. Not: isolation (also used, starts with \"i\"), confinement (lockdown), detention (by the police)."],["4c12av","Health: The surgeon gave him a general ______, so he was asleep during the operation. (starts with \"an\")","anaesthetic (anestesia): drug that stops you feeling pain; AmE anesthetic; general = unconscious, local = one area. Not: painkiller (for pain while awake), sedative (calms), antidote (against poison)."],["elinp3","Health: Take two ______ every four hours if the headache comes back. (starts with \"pai\")","painkillers (analgésicos): medicines that reduce pain. Not: antibiotics (kill bacteria), sedatives (calm or cause sleep), vaccines (prevent disease)."],["1l3zkfz","Health: The rescuers carried the injured climber down the mountain on a ______. (starts with \"st\")","stretcher (camilla): frame with cloth for carrying a person lying down. Not: crutch (to walk), wheelchair, stroller (AmE; BrE pushchair, for babies)."],["1t36gjj","Health: Her ankle ______ up so badly that she couldn't put her shoe on. (starts with \"sw\")","swelled (se hinchó): became bigger from fluid after an injury; adjective \"swollen\". Not: inflated (with air), grew, expanded (gases, businesses)."],["uoeasd","Health: He's been ______ up all night; he must have eaten something bad. (starts with \"th\")","throwing (up) (vomitando): informal for vomiting. Not: bringing up (also vomit, more polite; or raise a subject), throwing out (getting rid of), giving up (stopping)."],["ye0ifs","Health: My grandmother has ______ in her hands, so her joints are stiff and painful every morning. (starts with \"ar\")","arthritis (artritis): disease that makes the joints painful and stiff. Not: rheumatism (older, general word), cramp (sudden muscle pain), sprain (twisted joint)."],["1rpwbsp","Health: I woke up in the night with ______ in my calf and had to stretch the muscle. (starts with \"cr\")","cramp (calambre): sudden painful tightening of a muscle. Not: crutch (stick to walk), stitch (sharp pain in the side when running), spasm (formal)."],["1dxt4er","Health: I got a ______ in my side halfway through the race and had to slow down. (starts with \"st\")","stitch (flato): sharp pain in the side while running. Not: cramp (muscle tightening, often in the legs), stitches (threads in a wound), sprain."],["icm4pk","Health: The nurse checked my ______ by holding my wrist and counting the beats. (starts with \"pu\")","pulse (pulso): beat of the heart felt in the wrist or neck. Not: pressure (blood pressure, measured with a cuff), heartbeat (heard with a stethoscope), rhythm."],["18qbe3i","Health: If you are ______ to penicillin, tell the nurse before the injection. (starts with \"al\")","allergic (alérgico): reacting badly to a substance; \"allergic to\". Not: sensitive (milder), intolerant (food, digestion: lactose-intolerant), immune (not affected)."],["1uue1wv","Health: The doctor put him on a strict ______ to lower his cholesterol: no fried food, no cheese. (starts with \"di\")","diet (dieta, régimen): controlled eating plan; \"be on a diet\", \"go on a diet\". Not: regime (government), menu, nutrition (the process of feeding)."],["jkowyd","Work: Have you thought about a career in the ______ service, working for a government ministry? (starts with \"ci\")","civil (service) (función pública): the people who work in public administration. Not: civic (citizens and towns: civic duty, civic centre), national, governmental."],["19gyos7","Work: The factory closed and 300 workers were ______ off. (starts with \"la\")","laid (off) (despedidos por falta de trabajo): dismissed because there is no work, not for a fault. Not: fired or sacked (for a fault), resigned (left by choice), retired (stopped at the end of a career)."],["8uayp6","Work: He was ______ for stealing from the till. (starts with \"sa\")","sacked (despedido): informal BrE for dismissed for a fault; AmE fired. Not: laid off (no work for him), resigned (he chose to go), made redundant (his job no longer exists)."],["187s2lf","Work: After twenty years at the bank, she ______ to start her own business. (starts with \"res\")","resigned (dimitió, renunció): left a job by choice. Not: retired (stopped working because of age), withdrew, retreated (moved back)."],["glqfyj","Work: My grandfather ______ at 65 and now spends his days in the garden. (starts with \"ret\")","retired (se jubiló): stopped working because of age. Not: resigned (left one job by choice), withdrew, quit (informal: left a job)."],["esq8ug","Work: With unemployment so high, there were 400 ______ for just two jobs. (starts with \"ap\")","applicants (solicitantes, aspirantes): people who apply for something. Not: candidates (also used, often after shortlisting), employees (already hired), aspirants (rare)."],["14iu4x3","Work: All ______ must wear their badges inside the building; visitors get a temporary pass. (starts with \"em\")","employees (empleados): people paid to work for someone. Not: employers (the company or boss who pays), employment (having work), staff (a group noun)."],["9qggn4","Work: My ______ pays for my training courses and gives me 25 days' holiday a year. (starts with \"em\")","employer (empresa, empleador): the person or company that pays you. Not: employee (the worker), employment, boss (informal, starts with \"b\")."],["1x6kne7","Work: She earns a good ______ of 45,000 euros a year. (starts with \"sa\")","salary (sueldo): fixed yearly pay, usually paid monthly, for professional jobs. Not: wage (by the hour, day or week), fee (for a professional service), income (all the money you receive)."],["xbez38","Work: Cleaners here are paid a weekly ______ of 400 euros. (starts with \"wa\")","wage (jornal, sueldo semanal): pay by the hour, day or week. Not: salary (yearly, professional), fare (price of a ticket), fee."],["cvuesq","Work: The lawyer charges a ______ of 200 euros an hour. (starts with \"fe\")","fee (honorarios, tarifa): money paid for a professional service or to join something. Not: fare (transport ticket), toll (to use a road or bridge), wage."],["1kw9sfy","Work: Because the business made a loss, staff will not get a Christmas ______ this year. (starts with \"bo\")","bonus (paga extra, prima): extra money on top of normal pay. Not: tip (extra money for service in a bar), reward (for finding or helping), prize (for winning)."],["bd9x2a","Work: In Spain, waiters don't expect a large ______; leaving the small change is enough. (starts with \"ti\")","tip (propina): extra money for service. Not: bonus (paid by the employer), fee, change (money returned after paying)."],["1o704kl","Work: Retired people receive a state ______ every month. (starts with \"pe\")","pension (pensión): regular money paid after retirement. Not: allowance (money for a purpose, or pocket money), subsidy (government money to a business), grant."],["94emi","Work: Students from poorer families can apply for a ______ to cover their fees; it does not have to be paid back. (starts with \"gr\")","grant (beca, subvención): money given for a purpose, not repaid. Not: loan (repaid), scholarship (for merit), allowance."],["lif5nb","Work: We took out a 25-year ______ to buy our flat. (starts with \"mo\")","mortgage (hipoteca): loan to buy property. Not: loan (general word), rent (paid to a landlord), deposit (first payment, or money left as security)."],["1bxfmlj","Work: Every month I pay the ______ to my landlord on the first day. (starts with \"re\")","rent (alquiler): money paid to live in or use a property. Not: rental (the act or the thing rented), lease (the contract), mortgage."],["w82ht2","Work: The bank charges 4 % ______ on the loan. (starts with \"in\")","interest (interés): money paid for borrowing. Not: benefit (advantage, or state payments), profit (what a business earns), rate (the percentage itself)."],["mcv59z","Work: After the factory closed, he lived on unemployment ______ for six months. (starts with \"be\")","benefit (prestación, subsidio): state money for people who need help; AmE welfare. Not: profit (business gain), interest, pension (after retirement)."],["1cj1x4m","Work: The company made a ______ of two million euros last year, so the shareholders are happy. (starts with \"pro\")","profit (beneficio, ganancia): money earned after costs. Not: benefit (advantage or state payment; false friend \"beneficio\"), income, earnings (what a person is paid)."],["1096a0d","Work: Many shops went ______ during the crisis and closed for good. (starts with \"ba\")","bankrupt (en quiebra): unable to pay debts. Not: broke (informal: a person with no money now), insolvent (formal, starts with \"in\"), ruined."],["vv8hos","Work: The car is a ______ at that price: it's worth twice as much. (starts with \"ba\")","bargain (ganga, chollo): something bought for less than its value. Not: offer (a price reduction), sale (period of low prices), deal (agreement; \"a good deal\")."],["2cqzzh","Work: The shoes fell apart after a week, so I asked for a ______. (starts with \"ref\")","refund (reembolso, devolución del dinero): money given back. Not: receipt (proof of payment), reimbursement (formal, of expenses), discount (price cut before paying)."],["1ydmi6w","Work: Keep the ______ in case you need to return the shoes. (starts with \"rec\")","receipt (ticket, recibo): paper proving you paid. Not: recipe (cooking instructions; false friend \"receta\"), prescription (doctor's order), invoice (bill sent by a business)."],["10ke5mm","Work: He was ______ to manager after only two years in the company. (starts with \"pro\")","promoted (ascendido): given a higher position. Not: ascended (climbed, formal), raised (a salary is raised, a person is promoted), upgraded (equipment, seats)."],["yy9cf1","Work: I asked my boss for a pay ______, but she said the budget was frozen. (BrE, starts with \"ri\")","rise (aumento de sueldo): BrE \"a pay rise\"; AmE \"a raise\". Not: raising (the action), increment (formal), growth."],["1ikq9bx","Work: He has never worked in an office, but he's very skilled at his ______: he's an electrician. (starts with \"tr\")","trade (oficio): skilled job done with the hands (plumber, electrician, carpenter). Not: career (long professional path; false friend \"carrera\"), profession (needs a degree: law, medicine), labour."],["1ot64i6","Work: Water is pouring from the pipe under the sink; I'll call a ______. (starts with \"pl\")","plumber (fontanero). Not: electrician, bricklayer (albañil, builds walls), locksmith (locks and keys)."],["1lgdxb6","Work: I locked myself out, so I had to call a ______ to open the door. (starts with \"lo\")","locksmith (cerrajero): makes and repairs locks. Not: blacksmith (herrero, shapes iron in a forge), goldsmith, plumber."],["1ei4y8g","Work: The ______ in the village still makes iron gates and tools by hand in his forge. (starts with \"bl\")","blacksmith (herrero): shapes iron by heating it. Not: locksmith (locks), farrier (fits horseshoes), silversmith."],["1atkhlm","Work: My suit was too long in the sleeves, so a ______ altered it for me. (starts with \"ta\")","tailor (sastre): makes and alters suits and coats. Not: seamstress (sews and alters, especially dresses), dressmaker (makes women's clothes), designer."],["vab0wh","Work: The ______ shortened the wedding dress and took it in at the waist. (starts with \"se\")","seamstress (costurera, modista): woman who sews and alters clothes. Not: tailor (suits), furrier (fur coats), weaver (makes cloth on a loom)."],["kwdu21","Work: My shoes need new heels; I'll take them to the ______. (starts with \"co\")","cobbler (zapatero remendón): repairs shoes. Not: shoemaker (makes them), tailor, saddler (horse equipment)."],["10ly9ex","Work: The ______ re-covered our old sofa in a new fabric. (starts with \"up\")","upholsterer (tapicero): covers chairs and sofas with fabric and padding. Not: carpenter (works wood), decorator (paints and papers walls), tailor."],["1ik9d8w","Work: The ______ makes and sells mink and fox coats in a small shop near the station. (starts with \"fu\")","furrier (peletero): makes or sells fur clothing. Not: tanner (prepares leather), seamstress, saddler."],["3ap00b","Work: In the craft market, local ______ sell handmade pottery and jewellery. (starts with \"ar\")","artisans (artesanos): skilled people who make things by hand. Not: artists (paint, sculpt), craftsmen (also fits, starts with \"cr\"), merchants (traders)."],["ww5hai","Work: The school ______ keeps the building clean and repairs broken windows. (starts with \"ca\")","caretaker (conserje, bedel): BrE person who looks after a building; AmE janitor (AmE caretaker = someone who looks after a sick person). Not: porter (carries luggage), concierge, guard."],["iqjgk2","Work: She works ______: three days a week, mornings only. (starts with \"pa\")","part-time (a tiempo parcial). Not: full-time, overtime (extra hours), half-time (break in a match)."],["eor34","Work: I had to work ______ every evening this week to finish the report, so I'll be paid extra. (starts with \"ov\")","overtime (horas extra). Not: extra time (football), part-time, overwork (too much work, unhealthy)."],["7qznbl","Work: The ______ for the job include a degree and three years' experience. (starts with \"req\")","requirements (requisitos). Not: requests (asking for something), requisites (rare), demands (strong requests)."],["v283e6","Work: Because his post no longer exists, he was made ______ and received compensation. (starts with \"re\")","redundant (despedido por supresión del puesto): BrE \"made redundant\". Not: unemployed (the state of having no job), dismissed (general), retired."],["6duydi","Work: The two banks will ______ next year to form the largest bank in the country. (starts with \"me\")","merge (fusionarse): join together into one. Not: fuse (physical things), join (needs an object), acquire (buy another company)."],["jfsx51","Work: Our ______ is in Madrid, but we have branches all over Spain. (starts with \"hea\")","headquarters (sede central): main office of an organisation. Not: branch (local office), seat (of government or parliament), premises (the building and land)."],["1hy9k2i","Clothes: I washed my wool jumper in hot water and it ______; now it fits my little sister. (starts with \"sh\")","shrank (encogió): past of shrink (shrink, shrank, shrunk). Not: reduced (prices, numbers), diminished (formal: importance, power), contracted (metals, muscles)."],["1vkcn2d","Clothes: My jeans have ______ after so many washes; they used to be dark blue. (starts with \"fa\")","faded (desteñido): lost colour. Not: discoloured (stained a different colour), bleached (made white on purpose), worn (damaged by use)."],["d2nbdu","Clothes: The museum has a collection of medieval ______, from silk robes to wool cloaks. (starts with \"ga\")","garments (prendas): formal, countable word for pieces of clothing. Not: cloths (pieces of fabric for cleaning), clothing (uncountable), attire (uncountable, formal)."],["1uevdq5","Clothes: Use a damp ______ to wipe the kitchen table. (starts with \"cl\")","cloth (trapo, paño): piece of fabric for cleaning; plural cloths. Not: clothes (what you wear, always plural), clothing, rag (old torn cloth)."],["1oqv481","Clothes: Formal ______ is required at the gala dinner: dark suits and evening dresses. (starts with \"at\")","attire (atuendo, vestimenta): formal, uncountable word for the clothes worn for an occasion. Not: garments (countable pieces), costume (for a play or a fancy-dress party), uniform."],["1trg790","Clothes: These trousers don't ______ me any more: they're too tight round the waist. (starts with \"fi\")","fit (quedar bien de talla): be the right size. Not: suit (look good on someone), match (same colour or style as another thing), go with."],["14xjvmc","Clothes: That colour really ______ you; you should wear it more often. (starts with \"su\")","suits (te favorece, te sienta bien): looks good on a person. Not: fits (right size), matches (same as another thing), agrees (with an opinion)."],["vaw7ac","Clothes: Your handbag ______ your shoes perfectly: they're exactly the same red. (starts with \"ma\")","matches (combina, hace juego con): is the same colour or pattern as. Not: suits (looks good on a person), fits (size), equals."],["13mcboc","Clothes: Could you ______ up my zip at the back? I can't reach it. (starts with \"do\")","do (up) (abrochar, subir): fasten a zip, buttons or a coat; opposite \"undo\". Not: put up, close up, fix up."],["iotkv1","Clothes: The ______ of my skirt has come down, so I'll sew it back up. (starts with \"he\")","hem (dobladillo): folded and sewn bottom edge of a garment; verb \"to hem\". Not: seam (line where two pieces are sewn together), sleeve (arm part), collar (neck part)."],["5gazw1","Clothes: The jacket ripped along the ______ under the arm, where the two pieces are sewn together. (starts with \"se\")","seam (costura): line where two pieces of fabric are sewn together. Not: hem (folded bottom edge), stitch (one pass of the needle), zip."],["xp4qcy","Clothes: The dress was too loose, so the seamstress took it ______ at the waist. (one word)","in (take in = estrechar): make a garment narrower. Not: take up (shorten), let out (make wider), take off (remove)."],["1d9xddb","Clothes: She wore a long silk ______ with a train for the wedding. (starts with \"go\")","gown (vestido largo de gala): long formal dress; also the robe of a judge or a graduate. Not: robe (loose garment: bathrobe), frock (old word for dress), costume."],["spgarm","Clothes: He looked very ______ in his new suit and tie. (BrE, starts with \"sm\")","smart (elegante, arreglado): BrE well dressed and tidy; AmE smart = intelligent. Not: elegant (stronger), clever (intelligent), formal."],["1n33i17","Clothes: After the long flight he looked ______: his hair was a mess and his shirt was dirty. (starts with \"sc\")","scruffy (desaliñado): untidy and dirty in appearance. Not: shabby (old and worn: clothes, places), casual (relaxed, not formal), messy (starts with \"m\")."],["18yhd5v","Clothes: The restaurant lent him a tie because it has a strict ______ code. (starts with \"dr\")","dress (code) (código de vestimenta): rules about what to wear. Not: clothes code, uniform, etiquette (rules of polite behaviour)."],["lv6kl9","Clothes: I never iron my linen shirts, so they're always ______. (starts with \"cr\")","creased (arrugado): with lines from folding or crushing; also \"wrinkled\". Not: crumpled (badly crushed, like paper), folded (neatly bent), wrinkled (starts with \"w\")."],["deqfma","Clothes: Tie your shoe ______ or you'll trip over them. (starts with \"la\")","laces (cordones): strings that tie shoes. Not: strings, ties, straps (bands that fasten with a buckle)."],["1aw3olu","Clothes: The ______ on my belt broke, so my trousers kept falling down. (starts with \"bu\")","buckle (hebilla): metal fastener at the end of a belt. Not: button, clasp (on jewellery or a bag), hook."],["hu6obr","Clothes: She has a ______ complexion and burns easily in the sun. (starts with \"fa\")","fair (claro de piel): light skin or hair. Not: pale (white because ill or tired), blond (hair only), clear (without spots)."],["14xgoku","Clothes: He started going ______ at thirty, so now he shaves his head. (starts with \"ba\")","bald (calvo): losing the hair on the head. Not: bold (brave, confident), shaved (cut with a razor), hairless."],["4uyaen","Clothes: My father has a grey ______ but no beard. (starts with \"mo\")","moustache (bigote): hair above the upper lip; AmE mustache. Not: beard (chin and cheeks), sideburns (patillas), stubble (short growth of a few days)."],["o3idxr","Clothes: He hadn't shaved for three days, and dark ______ covered his chin. (starts with \"st\")","stubble (barba de pocos días). Not: beard (full growth), moustache, bristles (on a brush)."],["1u0c9a4","Clothes: She is tall and ______, with the graceful build of a dancer. (starts with \"sle\")","slender (esbelta): thin in an attractive way. Not: skinny (too thin, informal), slim (also fits, starts with \"sli\"), lean (thin and fit)."],["1mcb9g7","Clothes: He's rather ______ these days; the doctor told him to eat less and exercise more. (starts with \"ov\")","overweight (con sobrepeso): heavier than is healthy; polite. Not: fat (direct, can offend), obese (medical, very overweight), plump (pleasantly round)."],["1rei5gk","Clothes: The ______ are on: everything in the shop is half price this week. (starts with \"sa\")","sales (rebajas): period when shops lower their prices. Not: offers (single price reductions), discounts, bargains (the cheap items themselves)."],["8ldw21","Clothes: You can try the dress on in the ______ room at the back of the shop. (starts with \"fi\")","fitting (room) (probador): AmE dressing room. Not: changing room (sports centres; BrE shops too, starts with \"ch\"), trying room, cabin."],["1xeiskp","Clothes: She's wearing a woolly ______ over her shirt because it's cold. (BrE, starts with \"ju\")","jumper (jersey): BrE knitted top pulled over the head; AmE sweater. Not: jersey (football shirt; also a jumper, old BrE), cardigan (opens at the front with buttons), jump suit."],["1v2d2hl","Clothes: A ______ is a knitted jacket that you fasten with buttons at the front. (starts with \"ca\")","cardigan (rebeca, chaqueta de punto). Not: jumper (pulled over the head), blazer (smart jacket, often school or club), waistcoat (sleeveless; AmE vest)."],["1qh5wu4","Clothes: In Britain, the sleeveless garment worn under a suit jacket is a ______; in the United States it is a vest. (starts with \"wa\")","waistcoat (chaleco): AmE vest. Not: vest (BrE: underwear worn under a shirt), jacket, blazer."],["18645x9","Clothes: He spilt coffee on his shirt and it left a ______ that won't wash out. (starts with \"st\")","stain (mancha). Not: spot (small mark, or a pimple), mark (starts with \"m\"), dirt (uncountable)."],["zs3f2k","Transport: My ______ are almost bald; I need new ones before the long drive. (BrE spelling, starts with \"ty\")","tyres (neumáticos): BrE tyres, AmE tires. Not: wheels (the whole round part, including the metal rim), rims, tubes."],["grpb5y","Transport: We got a ______ tyre on the motorway and had to change it on the hard shoulder. (starts with \"fl\")","flat (pinchado): a flat tyre; BrE also \"a puncture\". Not: empty, deflated (formal), broken."],["11fh1po","Transport: A stone hit the ______ and cracked the glass in front of the driver. (BrE, starts with \"wi\")","windscreen (parabrisas): BrE; AmE windshield. Not: wing mirror (side mirror), window (side glass), wiper (limpiaparabrisas)."],["19wh2ij","Transport: I clipped a parked van and broke my ______ mirror, so I couldn't see the cyclist beside me. (BrE, starts with \"wi\")","wing (mirror) (retrovisor lateral): BrE; AmE side mirror. Not: rear-view mirror (inside, in the centre), window, wing (body panel over a wheel)."],["3g9rwr","Transport: Open the ______ and check the oil level in the engine. (BrE, starts with \"bo\")","bonnet (capó): BrE; AmE hood. Not: boot (luggage space), bumper, hood (BrE: folding roof of a convertible)."],["13gi2sn","Transport: Put the suitcases in the ______; there's plenty of room. (BrE, starts with \"bo\")","boot (maletero): BrE; AmE trunk. Not: bonnet (engine cover), glove box (guantera), roof rack (baca)."],["zjmhp3","Transport: The car behind hit my rear ______ at the traffic lights, but nobody was hurt. (starts with \"bu\")","bumper (parachoques). Not: boot, number plate (matrícula; AmE license plate), wing."],["sfttwa","Transport: The police officer asked to see my ______ licence and insurance documents. (BrE, starts with \"dr\")","driving (licence) (carnet de conducir): BrE; AmE driver's license. Not: driver licence, conduct licence (calque), driving permit."],["16zdrv1","Transport: Fasten your ______ belt before we set off. (starts with \"se\")","seat (belt) (cinturón de seguridad). Not: security belt (calque \"seguridad\"), safety belt (old, less common), waist belt."],["6og7yx","Transport: The lorry broke ______ on the motorway and caused a long queue. (one word)","down (break down = averiarse): stop working (machines, cars). Not: break up (end a relationship), break out (war, fire, escape), break in (enter by force)."],["11fhn5w","Transport: The accident caused a ten-kilometre ______ on the motorway. (BrE, starts with \"ta\")","tailback (retención, cola de coches): BrE long line of slow traffic. Not: traffic jam (general, starts with \"tr\"), queue (people, also cars), congestion (the general state)."],["1mwm4l4","Transport: We stopped at a ______ station to fill up and buy snacks. (BrE, starts with \"pe\")","petrol (station) (gasolinera): AmE gas station. Not: gas station (AmE), service station (on a motorway, wider), fuel pump."],["mxdfpm","Transport: Slow down: the ______ limit here is 50 km/h. (starts with \"sp\")","speed (limit) (límite de velocidad). Not: velocity (physics), rate, maximum."],["1u5ky6d","Transport: The driver was ______ over by the police for not wearing a seat belt. (starts with \"pu\")","pulled (over) (le hizo parar la policía): the police made the driver stop at the side of the road. Not: pulled up (stopped the car yourself), pulled out (moved into traffic), pulled in (moved to the side to stop)."],["1q607lu","Transport: You have to pay a ______ to cross the bridge: two euros per car. (starts with \"to\")","toll (peaje): money paid to use a road or bridge. Not: fare (passenger ticket price), fee (for a service), tax."],["xif33","Transport: The bus ______ has gone up again: a single ticket now costs two euros. (starts with \"fa\")","fare (tarifa, precio del billete): price of a journey on public transport. Not: fee (professional service), toll (road), fair (just; or a funfair)."],["1a2v16q","Transport: Turn left at the ______ and take the second exit. (starts with \"ro\")","roundabout (rotonda): BrE; AmE traffic circle. Not: crossroads (where two roads cross), junction (any place where roads meet), ring road (road round a city)."],["82lomd","Transport: Pedestrians should cross at the zebra ______. (BrE, starts with \"cr\")","crossing (paso de cebra): BrE zebra crossing; AmE crosswalk. Not: crossroads (where roads meet), crosswalk (AmE), pass."],["8d4m5e","Transport: The lorry driver didn't see the cyclist because she was in his ______ spot. (starts with \"bl\")","blind (spot) (ángulo muerto). Not: dead angle (calque), dark spot, hidden zone."],["8hjv4k","Transport: Press the ______ gently as you go down the hill. (starts with \"br\")","brake (freno): pedal that slows the car; verb \"to brake\". Not: break (romper, same sound), clutch (embrague), accelerator."],["11fbod8","Transport: In a manual car, press the ______ before you change gear. (starts with \"cl\")","clutch (embrague). Not: brake, gear lever (palanca de cambios), accelerator."],["s9nnt0","Transport: The ______ is the pedal that makes the car go faster. (starts with \"ac\")","accelerator (acelerador): AmE also gas pedal. Not: brake, clutch, throttle (aircraft, motorbikes)."],["x0199x","Transport: Switch on your ______ before you turn so other drivers know where you're going. (BrE, starts with \"in\")","indicator (intermitente): BrE; AmE turn signal or blinker. Not: headlights (faros), hazard lights (all flash together), sidelights."],["pwwqq7","Transport: It's getting dark: switch on your ______. (starts with \"hea\")","headlights (faros delanteros). Not: indicators, fog lights, brake lights (red, at the back)."],["8jj18t","Transport: We missed the last bus, so we had to ______ a taxi in the street. (starts with \"ha\")","hail (parar con la mano): wave to make a taxi stop. Not: call (by phone), catch (take: \"catch a bus\"), stop (starts with \"st\")."],["1yq3103","Transport: We travelled from London to Edinburgh by ______, a long-distance bus that was cheaper than the train. (BrE, starts with \"co\")","coach (autocar): BrE long-distance bus. Not: bus (local), carriage (one part of a train; BrE also \"coach\"), car."],["jks0wh","Transport: Hold the steering ______ with both hands. (starts with \"wh\")","wheel (steering wheel = volante). Not: tyre (rubber part), rim, handlebars (bicycle)."],["1h1tlpw","Transport: He was fined for ______ in a bus lane outside the station. (starts with \"pa\")","parking (aparcar): leaving a vehicle somewhere. Not: stopping (briefly), stationing (troops), waiting."],["5vz6hf","Transport: Drivers must give ______ to traffic already on the roundabout. (BrE, starts with \"wa\")","way (give way = ceder el paso): AmE yield. Not: give pass, give priority (also \"have priority\"), give room."],["1ho66vw","Transport: On a motorway you may stop on the hard ______ only in an emergency. (BrE, starts with \"sh\")","shoulder (hard shoulder = arcén): BrE; AmE shoulder. Not: verge (grass edge of a road), pavement (acera), lay-by (area at the side of a road for stopping)."],["ds3pjp","Transport: Keep off the road and walk on the ______. (BrE, starts with \"pa\")","pavement (acera): BrE; AmE sidewalk (AmE pavement = road surface). Not: path (track in the country or a park), platform (andén), kerb (bordillo; AmE curb)."],["q4wbjl","Sport: The tennis players walked out onto the centre ______ at Wimbledon. (starts with \"co\")","court (pista): tennis, basketball, squash. Not: pitch (football, rugby, cricket), rink (ice), course (golf, racing)."],["bxh77q","Sport: The fans ran onto the football ______ after the final whistle. (BrE, starts with \"pi\")","pitch (campo): BrE for football, rugby, cricket; AmE field. Not: court (tennis), field (starts with \"f\"), ground (the whole stadium, BrE)."],["3dn0pl","Sport: We went ice skating at the new ______ in the shopping centre. (starts with \"ri\")","rink (pista de hielo): ice skating, ice hockey. Not: track (running), court, ring (boxing)."],["1vqvq7m","Sport: He plays eighteen holes at the golf ______ every Sunday. (starts with \"co\")","course (campo de golf); also racecourse. Not: court (tennis), pitch (football), field."],["118w6xm","Sport: The two boxers stepped into the ______ for the final round. (starts with \"ri\")","ring (cuadrilátero): boxing, wrestling. Not: rink (ice), court, arena (the whole building)."],["ju2y4u","Sport: The athletes warmed up on the running ______ before the 400 metres. (starts with \"tr\")","track (pista de atletismo). Not: course (golf), lane (each runner's strip), court."],["ib9xvg","Sport: The ______ blew his whistle and showed the defender a red card. (starts with \"re\")","referee (árbitro): football, rugby, boxing, basketball. Not: umpire (tennis, cricket, baseball), judge (gymnastics, skating), linesman (assistant on the line)."],["yzwctp","Sport: In tennis, the ______ sits in a high chair and calls the score. (starts with \"um\")","umpire (juez de silla). Not: referee (football, boxing), judge, line judge."],["ijmcvw","Sport: The defender was sent ______ after a second yellow card. (one word)","off (sent off = expulsado). Not: sent out, sent away, sent down (sent to prison, or relegated)."],["hc1no3","Sport: Real Madrid ______ Barcelona 3-1 in last night's match. (starts with \"be\")","beat (ganó a, derrotó): beat a person or team. Not: won (you win a match, game or prize, not a team), defeated (also correct, starts with \"d\"), gained."],["4y8itz","Sport: Spain ______ the World Cup in 2010. (starts with \"wo\")","won (ganó): win a competition, game or prize. Not: beat (an opponent), earned (money by working), gained (weight, experience)."],["1mqc4f2","Sport: The match ended in a 2-2 ______. (starts with \"dr\")","draw (empate): BrE; AmE tie. Not: tie (AmE; BrE a cup match), equal, deuce (40-40 in tennis)."],["8m9kfi","Sport: After finishing bottom of the league, the club was ______ to the second division. (starts with \"re\")","relegated (descendido). Not: promoted (moved up), demoted (people, in a job), dropped (a player left out of the team)."],["m3dms5","Sport: Thousands of ______ cheered when the home team came out of the tunnel. (starts with \"sp\")","spectators (espectadores): people watching a sport live. Not: audience (theatre, TV, concert), viewers (TV), public (people in general)."],["1jfecl9","Sport: The team's ______ makes them train twice a day and decides the tactics. (starts with \"co\")","coach (entrenador): trains a team or athlete; in British football often \"manager\". Not: trainer (BrE trainers = sports shoes), captain (player who leads on the pitch), instructor."],["g4t7z3","Sport: She ______ the world record for the 100 metres by a tenth of a second. (starts with \"br\")","broke (batió): break a record. Not: beat (also used, starts with \"be\"), won, overcame."],["7zw1f3","Sport: Over 200 runners will ______ part in the marathon on Sunday. (starts with \"ta\")","take (part) (participar). Not: make part, do part, have part."],["1681e0x","Sport: The two finalists will ______ for a prize of a million euros. (starts with \"co\")","compete (competir): try to win against others. Not: contest (formal: a decision, an election), challenge, dispute."],["akj2h3","Sport: Bring your ______ and a towel; we're going to the gym after work. (BrE, starts with \"tr\")","trainers (zapatillas de deporte): BrE; AmE sneakers. Not: trainer (person who trains you), sneakers (AmE), slippers (worn at home)."],["1viswuo","Sport: The final was 1-1 after extra time, so it went to ______. (starts with \"pe\")","penalties (penaltis): BrE also \"a penalty shoot-out\". Not: free kicks, corners, fouls."],["1pjogzn","Sport: He's a keen ______: he goes fishing at the lake every weekend. (starts with \"an\")","angler (pescador de caña): person who fishes with a rod for pleasure. Not: fisherman (general, often professional), hunter, sailor."],["1k4i1y9","Sport: The away team ______ an equaliser in the last minute. (starts with \"sc\")","scored (marcó). Not: marked (marking a player = defending; false friend \"marcar\"), got, made."],["15es9aq","Sport: Each runner must stay in his own ______ during the 400 metres. (starts with \"la\")","lane (calle, carril). Not: track (the whole running area), line, row."],["1uduph8","Sport: The two captains shook hands just before ______-off. (starts with \"ki\")","kick (kick-off = saque inicial). Not: start-off, take-off (aircraft), kick-out."],["z7gfyn","Sport: He has been called up to the national ______ for the first time. (starts with \"sq\")","squad (convocatoria, plantilla): group of players from which a team is chosen. Not: team (the players on the pitch), staff, crew (ship, aircraft)."],["ibtp5b","Society: Years of war destroyed the harvests and caused a ______ that killed thousands. (starts with \"fa\")","famine (hambruna): extreme lack of food over a large area. Not: drought (no rain: a possible cause), hunger (the feeling; also general), starvation (suffering or dying from lack of food)."],["1829csa","Society: After two years without rain, the ______ destroyed crops across the region. (starts with \"dr\")","drought (sequía). Not: famine (lack of food), flood, heatwave (period of very hot weather), draught (BrE cold air in a room)."],["hegs7u","Society: Heavy rain made the river ______ its banks and flood the village. (starts with \"bu\")","burst (desbordarse): a river bursts its banks. Not: break (not used with banks), overflow (also used, without \"its banks\"), exceed."],["1drlkuc","Society: Thousands of people were ______ from their homes before the hurricane arrived. (starts with \"ev\")","evacuated (evacuados): moved away from danger. Not: evicted (forced out by a landlord or a court), expelled (from a school or country), emptied."],["d67q4s","Society: The south of the city is its most ______ area, with high unemployment and poor housing. (starts with \"dep\")","deprived (desfavorecido): lacking money, housing and services. Not: depraved (morally evil), depressed (sad; or an area with little economic activity), poor (starts with \"p\")."],["1lt61ae","Society: Decades of drought have left the region ______, with incomes far below the national average. (starts with \"imp\")","impoverished (empobrecido): made poor. Not: affluent, wealthy, loaded (all mean rich: the clue \"below average\" rules them out)."],["s53648","Society: She grew up in an ______ suburb full of large houses and expensive cars. (starts with \"af\")","affluent (acomodado, adinerado): formal for rich. Not: effluent (liquid waste), influential (has power over others), fluent (in a language)."],["1vt1czz","Society: ______ of the new law say it will protect workers; its critics say it will cost jobs. (starts with \"pro\")","Proponents (defensores, partidarios): people who argue for an idea. Not: opponents, detractors, sceptics (all against it)."],["1pejv7o","Society: ______ of the plan, including several environmental groups, say it will damage the coast. (starts with \"op\")","Opponents (detractores, opositores): people against an idea. Not: proponents and supporters (for it), competitors (business, sport), rivals."],["145iw0e","Society: Next Sunday the country goes to the ______ to elect a new parliament. (starts with \"po\")","polls (urnas): \"go to the polls\" = vote in an election. Not: urns (for ashes), votes, ballots (\"the ballot box\", starts with \"b\")."],["1hqiv5g","Society: Only 55 % of registered voters ______ a vote in the referendum. (starts with \"ca\")","cast (emitieron, votaron): \"cast a vote\". Not: threw, put, made."],["1i33le7","Society: The government plans to ______ the old law and replace it with a fairer one. (starts with \"rep\")","repeal (derogar): officially end a law. Not: abolish (end a system or practice, starts with \"ab\"), revoke (a licence or permission), repel (push back an attack)."],["dazadf","Society: Many countries ______ slavery in the nineteenth century. (starts with \"ab\")","abolished (abolieron): officially ended a system or practice. Not: repealed (a specific law), cancelled (an event), forbade (prohibited)."],["1xs56rk","Society: The two men were ______ on suspicion of drug smuggling. (starts with \"ar\")","arrested (detenidos): \"arrested on suspicion of\". Not: detained (held, often without charge, starts with \"d\"), charged (formally accused after arrest), convicted (found guilty)."],["12cdyxf","Society: After a three-week trial, the jury found him ______ of fraud. (starts with \"gu\")","guilty (culpable): \"find someone guilty of\". Not: culpable (formal: deserving blame), responsible, innocent."],["c7wte6","Society: The judge ______ him to five years in prison. (starts with \"se\")","sentenced (condenó): \"sentence someone to\" a punishment. Not: condemned (strong disapproval, or condemned to death), convicted (found guilty, not the punishment), judged."],["38uy8h","Society: He was ______ of murder, but the verdict was overturned on appeal. (starts with \"co\")","convicted (declarado culpable): officially found guilty. Not: convinced (persuaded), sentenced (given the punishment), accused (charged, not yet judged)."],["76l636","Society: Two armed men ______ the bank and escaped with two million euros. (starts with \"ro\")","robbed (atracaron): rob a place or a person. Not: stole (steal a thing: they stole the money), burgled (a house, when nobody is in), mugged (a person in the street)."],["qwfx0q","Society: Someone ______ my wallet on the metro this morning. (starts with \"st\")","stole (robó): steal a thing. Not: robbed (a person or a place: someone robbed me), burgled, mugged."],["10rkt7h","Society: Our house was ______ while we were on holiday; they took the TV and the jewellery. (BrE, starts with \"bu\")","burgled (robaron en casa): BrE; AmE burglarized. Not: robbed (a person or a bank), stolen (things), broken (damaged)."],["1o6emq","Society: An old man was ______ in the park: two youths threatened him and took his phone. (starts with \"mu\")","mugged (atracado): attacked and robbed in the street. Not: robbed (general), burgled (a house), kidnapped (taken away by force)."],["i8gnmk","Society: The ______ told the court she had seen the defendant leave the building at midnight. (starts with \"wi\")","witness (testigo). Not: spectator (watches sport), bystander (present at an event but not involved), testifier."],["jy4ul3","Society: The police found new ______ linking the suspect to the crime. (starts with \"ev\")","evidence (pruebas): uncountable; \"a piece of evidence\". Not: evidences (no plural), proofs (maths, printing), clues (help to solve a mystery)."],["1arkqo9","Society: Both ______ in the dispute agreed to settle out of court. (starts with \"pa\")","parties (partes): people or groups in a legal agreement or dispute. Not: parts, sides (starts with \"s\"), members."],["1s6lgse","Society: The airline paid her 600 euros in ______ for the cancelled flight. (starts with \"com\")","compensation (indemnización): money paid for loss or harm. Not: refund (money back for what you paid), reward, damages (court award, starts with \"d\")."],["1jd8xfi","Society: Smoking is ______ in all public buildings. (starts with \"ba\")","banned (prohibido): forbidden by law or a rule. Not: forbidden (formal, or by parents), illegal (starts with \"il\"), barred (people kept out of a place)."],["owfama","Society: The new law comes into ______ on 1 January. (starts with \"fo\")","force (vigor): \"come into force\" = start to apply. Not: effect (\"take effect\"), power, vigour (energy)."],["12m635q","Society: Protesters ______ against the new tax outside parliament. (starts with \"de\")","demonstrated (se manifestaron). Not: manifested (showed: an illness or a feeling; false friend \"manifestarse\"), protested (starts with \"p\"), showed."],["14saxjh","Society: The ______ rate has fallen to 12 %, the lowest in a decade. (starts with \"un\")","unemployment (desempleo, paro). Not: unemployed (the people), redundancy (losing a job because it is no longer needed), jobless (adjective)."],["3cbvax","Society: The ______ of the town have voted against the new motorway. (starts with \"re\")","residents (vecinos, residentes): people who live in a place. Not: neighbours (people next door), inhabitants (formal: of a country or region), tenants (rent their home)."],["19s6jb4","Society: A ______ is someone who has left their country to escape war or persecution. (starts with \"re\")","refugee (refugiado). Not: immigrant (comes to live in a new country for any reason), emigrant (leaves their own country), asylum seeker (has asked for protection, not yet granted)."],["1wai9kq","Society: Thousands of ______ left Spain in the 1960s to work in Germany and Switzerland. (starts with \"em\")","emigrants (emigrantes): people leaving their own country. Not: immigrants (arriving in a new country), migrants (general), expatriates (professionals living abroad)."],["18huc8g","Society: The council has promised more ______ housing for young families who cannot afford market rents. (starts with \"so\")","social (housing) (vivienda social, de protección oficial): AmE public housing. Not: council housing (BrE, starts with \"c\"), public, popular."],["1c1bfo5","Society: The ______ pay gap means that women earn on average 10 % less than men. (starts with \"ge\")","gender (pay gap) (brecha salarial de género). Not: genre (type of film, music or book), generation gap (between young and old), sex gap."],["m7kf0r","Society: The country's population is ______: a third of the people are over 65. (starts with \"ag\")","ageing (envejeciendo): AmE aging. Not: elderly (describes people, polite), old, growing (getting bigger)."],["18596ps","Society: Many young people are ______ about politics and don't bother to vote. (starts with \"ap\")","apathetic (apáticos, indiferentes). Not: sympathetic (understanding; false friend \"simpático\"), pathetic (causing pity or contempt), passive."],["cerqob","Society: Thanks to strong ______ growth, unemployment fell for the third year in a row. (starts with \"ec\")","economic (económico): relating to the economy. Not: economical (cheap to run, not wasteful), economics (the science), economy (the system itself)."],["tr5hnb","Society: Our new car is very ______: it uses only four litres every 100 km. (starts with \"ec\")","economical (económico, que ahorra): cheap to run, not wasteful. Not: economic (relating to the economy), cheap (low price), efficient (starts with \"ef\")."],["jjktmo","Society: Every adult has a ______ duty to vote and to serve on a jury when called. (starts with \"ci\")","civic (cívico): relating to citizens and their town. Not: civil (civil service, civil war, civil rights), civilian (not in the armed forces), civilised (polite, advanced)."],["olzeoz","Society: The ______ population suffered most during the bombing; the soldiers were in shelters. (starts with \"ci\")","civilian (civil, no militar): not in the armed forces. Not: civic (citizens and towns), civil (civil service, civil war), civilised."],["iznflv","Society: Millions of people around the world live below the ______ line. (starts with \"po\")","poverty (pobreza): \"the poverty line\". Not: poorness (rare), poor (adjective), misery (great unhappiness; false friend \"miseria\")."],["1ktes55","People: I wouldn't call him a friend; he's more of an ______ from my old job. (starts with \"ac\")","acquaintance (conocido): someone you know slightly. Not: peer (person of the same age or status), colleague (works with you now, starts with \"co\"), ancestor."],["1mwraoz","People: Teenagers often care more about what their ______ think than about their parents' opinions. (starts with \"pe\")","peers (iguales, compañeros de su edad): people of the same age, group or status. Not: pairs (sets of two), equals, mates (informal friends)."],["1dxs8kd","People: My ______ came to Spain from Italy in the eighteenth century. (starts with \"an\")","ancestors (antepasados). Not: descendants (who come after you), predecessors (earlier holders of a job), antecessors (rare)."],["v34x5l","People: The new director is very different from her ______, who ran the company for twenty years. (starts with \"pre\")","predecessor (predecesor): previous holder of a job. Not: successor (the next one), ancestor (family), forerunner (earlier version of something)."],["k0o8fw","People: When the king died, his eldest son became his ______ on the throne. (starts with \"su\")","successor (sucesor): next holder of a job or title. Not: predecessor (the one before), heir (person who will inherit, starts with \"h\"), descendant."],["266v4y","People: I'm an only ______: I have no brothers or sisters. (starts with \"ch\")","child (hijo único). Not: unique child (calque), single child (rare), only son (says the sex, starts with \"so\")."],["o017q3","People: My brother and his girlfriend got ______ last week and plan to marry in June. (starts with \"en\")","engaged (prometidos). Not: compromised (put at risk; false friend \"comprometido\"), committed (dedicated, or in a serious relationship), promised."],["l7ri5e","People: She ______ after her mother: the same eyes, the same laugh. (starts with \"ta\")","takes (after) (se parece a): looks or behaves like an older relative. Not: looks after (cares for), looks like (also fits without \"after\"), takes over (takes control)."],["1ec9wzi","People: My sister and I ______ out over money and haven't spoken for a year. (starts with \"fe\")","fell (out) (nos peleamos): stopped being friends after an argument. Not: fell apart (broke into pieces), fell through (a plan failed), broke up (couples ending a relationship)."],["7akr5d","People: It was very ______ of you to remember my birthday. (starts with \"th\")","thoughtful (considerado, atento): showing care for others. Not: thoughtless (careless of others), pensive (thinking seriously, often sad), considerate (also fits, starts with \"co\")."],["1d7ag78","People: He's very ______: he cries at sad films and is easily hurt by criticism. (starts with \"sens\")","sensitive (sensible, susceptible): easily affected emotionally. Not: sensible (sensato: practical and reasonable; false friend), sensual, sentimental."],["1awzsjg","People: Taking an umbrella was a ______ decision; it rained all day. (starts with \"sens\")","sensible (sensato, prudente): practical and reasonable. Not: sensitive (easily hurt or affected), sensational, reasonable (starts with \"r\")."],["suzn6e","People: She is so ______ that she never gives up, even after failing the test three times. (starts with \"de\")","determined (decidido, resuelto): positive. Not: stubborn (refuses to change, negative), decided (clear: of an opinion or a result), obstinate."],["wevhm7","People: My grandfather is too ______ to change his mind once he has decided something. (starts with \"stu\")","stubborn (testarudo, terco): refuses to change, negative. Not: determined (positive), strict (makes others obey rules), steady (stable)."],["47rvdl","People: Our teacher is very ______: she never accepts homework handed in late. (starts with \"str\")","strict (estricto, exigente): makes others follow rules. Not: stubborn (won't change their own mind), severe (very bad: illness, weather), rigid."],["1n3fx36","People: He's so ______ that he never thinks about anyone but himself. (starts with \"sel\")","selfish (egoísta). Not: selfless (the opposite: thinks of others first), self-confident (sure of their abilities), self-conscious (embarrassed about how others see them)."],["61p5pw","People: Don't be so ______ about your new haircut: nobody is staring at you. (starts with \"self-c\")","self-conscious (cohibido, acomplejado): worried about how others see you. Not: self-confident (sure of yourself), conscious (awake, aware), conscientious (careful and hard-working)."],["attxkv","People: He is a ______ worker who checks every detail twice. (starts with \"con\")","conscientious (concienzudo): careful and hard-working. Not: conscious (aware, awake), conscience (noun: sense of right and wrong), consistent (always the same)."],["1q6gk0a","People: She's very ______: she always tells you exactly what she thinks, even when it hurts. (starts with \"bl\")","blunt (directo, brusco): says what they think without trying to be polite. Not: frank (honest, more positive), rude (impolite), sincere."],["swi2xg","People: My neighbour is so ______: he always wants to know who visits me and why. (starts with \"no\")","nosy (cotilla, fisgón): too interested in other people's lives; also nosey. Not: noisy (loud), curious (wanting to know, neutral), gossip (noun: the talk or the person)."],["oy3961","People: Don't be so ______: share the sweets with your brother. (starts with \"me\")","mean (tacaño; BrE also unkind): not wanting to spend or share. Not: stingy (starts with \"st\"), cheap (AmE informal; BrE low price), greedy (wants more for themselves)."],["7wi4b8","People: She's very ______ about her success and never boasts. (starts with \"mo\")","modest (modesto): does not talk proudly about themselves. Not: humble (also fits, starts with \"h\"), shy (nervous with people), moderate (not extreme)."],["1u4jvhz","People: He's very ______ at parties: he doesn't talk to anyone he doesn't know. (starts with \"sh\")","shy (tímido). Not: timid (easily frightened, starts with \"t\"), modest, reserved (starts with \"r\")."],["y3ntsl","People: My boss is so ______ that I never know how she will react to anything. (starts with \"unp\")","unpredictable (imprevisible). Not: unreliable (cannot be trusted to do things), unstable, unexpected (events, not people)."],["zw4bib","People: You can always count on Ana: she's completely ______. (starts with \"rel\")","reliable (fiable, de confianza). Not: reliant (dependent on someone), relevant (connected to the subject), credible (believable)."],["1mdy10w","People: Do you believe in that old ______ that a black cat brings bad luck? (starts with \"su\")","superstition (superstición). Not: curse (magic words that bring harm), myth (traditional story, or a false belief), legend."],["1q6ygxc","People: As the ______ goes, \"Don't count your chickens before they hatch\". (starts with \"sa\")","saying (refrán, dicho): \"as the saying goes\". Not: proverb (also fits, starts with \"pro\"), quote (exact words of someone), phrase."],["pewxij","People: I can't decide whether to take the job abroad or stay near my family: it's a real ______. (starts with \"di\")","dilemma (dilema): difficult choice between two options. Not: paradox (something that seems to contradict itself), problem, query (question)."],["1yw43bk","People: I had a ______ that she was lying, but I couldn't prove it. (starts with \"hu\")","hunch (corazonada, presentimiento): feeling based on intuition. Not: suspicion (also fits, starts with \"su\"), clue (piece of evidence), hint (indirect suggestion)."],["1oqakes","People: I ______ we'll need about two hours to get there, don't you think? (starts with \"re\")","reckon (creo, calculo): informal for \"think, suppose\". Not: reflect (think deeply), regard (consider: regard as), recognise (know again)."],["1nmjmil","People: My boss is so ______ in the mornings that nobody talks to her before her coffee. (starts with \"gru\")","grumpy (gruñón, malhumorado). Not: grim (serious and depressing), angry (at something particular), moody (changes mood often)."],["13oujnv","People: My grandmother is ______ but still very active: she walks five kilometres a day. (starts with \"el\")","elderly (mayor, anciano): polite word for old. Not: aged (formal, or \"aged 80\"), old-fashioned (not modern), ancient (very old things)."],["1g4dj0r","People: After their parents died, the children were ______ up by their grandparents. (starts with \"br\")","brought (up) (criados): cared for until adulthood. Not: grown up (became adults), raised (no \"up\", starts with \"r\"), educated (taught at school; false friend \"educado\")."],["1r1rzuz","People: She's a very well-______ girl: she always says please and thank you. (starts with \"ma\")","mannered (educada): \"well-mannered\" = polite. Not: well-educated (has studied a lot; false friend \"educado\"), well-behaved (starts with \"be\"), well-bred."],["3w1k5c","People: She's a real ______: she loves parties and meeting new people. (starts with \"ex\")","extrovert (extrovertida): outgoing person. Not: introvert, extravagant (spends too much; unusual), outgoing (adjective, starts with \"o\")."],["5u90z9","Home: ______ the potatoes before you boil them. (starts with \"pe\")","Peel (pelar): remove the skin of fruit and vegetables. Not: shell (hard case: eggs, nuts, prawns), skin (animals; also tomatoes), scale (fish)."],["jgu74s","Home: ______ the prawns and remove the black vein. (starts with \"sh\")","Shell (pelar marisco): remove the hard outer case of prawns, eggs, nuts. Not: peel (fruit, vegetables), husk, pod."],["1xp8ohi","Home: The fishmonger will ______ the fish for you, so you don't get scales all over the kitchen. (starts with \"sc\")","scale (escamar): remove the scales of a fish. Not: peel, skin (remove the skin), fillet (cut the flesh off the bones)."],["101vv7w","Home: In the old days, cooks had to ______ the chicken's feathers by hand before roasting it. (starts with \"pl\")","pluck (desplumar): pull out feathers. Not: peel, strip, pick."],["whpl6n","Home: This steak is so ______ I can hardly cut it. (starts with \"to\")","tough (duro): hard to cut or chew (meat). Not: hard (bread, cheese, stone), strong (taste, coffee), stiff (difficult to bend)."],["1vz2a1c","Home: This bread is ______: it was baked three days ago. (starts with \"st\")","stale (duro, pasado): no longer fresh (bread, cake). Not: off (milk, meat: gone bad), rotten (fruit, eggs: decayed), tough (meat)."],["1b0wk7y","Home: Don't drink the milk: it's gone ______. (BrE, starts with \"of\")","off (cortada, pasada): BrE gone bad (milk, meat, fish). Not: stale (bread), rotten (fruit, eggs), sour (also fits, starts with \"so\")."],["1gp3fh2","Home: The apples at the bottom of the box were ______ and had to be thrown away. (starts with \"ro\")","rotten (podridas). Not: stale (bread), mouldy (covered in mould, starts with \"mo\"), off (milk)."],["7l9xpl","Home: Our ______ is very strict: no pets and no parties after midnight. (starts with \"la\")","landlord (casero): person who rents out a home; a woman is a landlady. Not: tenant (person who rents), owner (general), host."],["1ndg8bx","Home: The ______ in the flat upstairs pay 800 euros a month in rent. (starts with \"te\")","tenants (inquilinos): people who rent a home. Not: landlords, lodgers (rent a room in the owner's home), occupants (whoever is inside)."],["exgmz3","Home: We live in a ______ house: we share one wall with the family next door. (starts with \"se\")","semi-detached (pareado). Not: detached (stands alone), terraced (in a row; AmE row house), bungalow (one floor)."],["zepn4q","Home: They bought a ______ house with a big garden; it shares no walls with any neighbour. (starts with \"de\")","detached (independiente, unifamiliar aislada). Not: semi-detached, terraced, isolated (far from other places)."],["kw0bh6","Home: We had to call a plumber because the kitchen ______ was blocked. (starts with \"si\")","sink (fregadero): the bathroom one is a washbasin. Not: basin (washbasin), tap (grifo; AmE faucet), drain (desagüe)."],["113q27z","Home: Turn off the ______ while you brush your teeth to save water. (BrE, starts with \"ta\")","tap (grifo): AmE faucet. Not: plug (tapón), hose (manguera), pipe (tubería)."],["1dsdta7","Home: We keep old furniture and boxes up in the ______, just under the roof. (starts with \"at\")","attic (desván): room just under the roof; also loft. Not: penthouse (expensive top-floor flat; Spanish \"ático\"), basement (below ground), cellar."],["1hh0zms","Home: The wine is stored in the ______, below the ground floor. (starts with \"ce\")","cellar (bodega, sótano): underground room for storage. Not: basement (living space below ground, starts with \"b\"), cellular, attic."],["1992tq8","Home: The builders are ______ the old farmhouse: new roof, new kitchen, new wiring. (starts with \"ren\")","renovating (reformando): repairing and improving an old building. Not: renewing (a contract, a passport), reforming (laws, systems; false friend \"reformar\"), restoring (back to the original state)."],["bo96eq","Home: Could you ______ the table? Dinner's almost ready. (starts with \"la\")","lay (poner): \"lay the table\" (also \"set\"). Not: put, lie (be horizontal), place."],["1i1maoh","Home: I cooked, so you're doing the ______-up tonight. (BrE, starts with \"wa\")","washing (washing-up = fregar los platos): BrE; AmE do the dishes. Not: washing (clothes), cleaning, dishwasher."],["a4cp5u","Home: I need to do the ______: I have no clean socks left. (starts with \"la\")","laundry (colada): washing clothes; BrE also \"the washing\". Not: washing-up (plates), cleaning (the house), dry cleaning."],["y7lg9","Home: ______ the onions finely and fry them in olive oil. (starts with \"ch\")","Chop (picar, trocear): cut into small pieces. Not: slice (thin flat pieces), grate (rub into tiny pieces: cheese, carrot), mince (meat through a machine)."],["i8u8p","Home: ______ some cheese over the pasta before serving. (starts with \"gr\")","Grate (rallar). Not: chop, slice, crush (press hard: garlic)."],["1br3pme","Home: Let the sauce ______ gently for twenty minutes without letting it boil hard. (starts with \"si\")","simmer (cocer a fuego lento). Not: boil (bubbles hard), stew (cook meat slowly in liquid), steam (cook over boiling water)."],["hgbnij","Home: Excuse me, could we have the ______, please? We'd like to pay. (BrE, starts with \"bi\")","bill (cuenta): AmE check. Not: count, note (BrE banknote), receipt (proof after paying)."],["k42td","Home: We ordered a three-______ meal: starter, main and dessert. (starts with \"co\")","course (plato): one part of a meal. Not: plate (what you eat from), dish (food prepared in a particular way), menu."],["1lq242o","Home: Paella is the most famous ______ from Valencia. (starts with \"di\")","dish (plato): food prepared in a particular way. Not: plate (the object), course (stage of a meal), recipe (instructions)."],["19u4cra","Home: Could you give me the ______ for this cake? It's delicious. (starts with \"rec\")","recipe (receta): instructions for cooking. Not: receipt (proof of payment), prescription (medicine), formula."],["enaog4","Home: Our flat is on the fifth floor and there's no ______, so we carry the shopping up the stairs. (BrE, starts with \"li\")","lift (ascensor): AmE elevator. Not: escalator (moving stairs), hoist (machine for lifting goods), elevator (AmE)."],["19yv780","Home: The kitchen comes with all the usual ______: a fridge, a dishwasher and an oven. (starts with \"ap\")","appliances (electrodomésticos). Not: applications (forms, software), devices (small electronic gadgets), furniture (uncountable: tables, chairs)."],["85y6ok","Home: We live in a quiet ______ outside the city, and most people here commute in by train. (starts with \"su\")","suburb (barrio residencial de las afueras). Not: outskirts (plural: \"on the outskirts\"), slum (very poor area), neighbourhood (starts with \"n\")."],["pdrwp6","Nature: Soya is the most important ______ in Brazil, and farmers export most of it. (starts with \"cr\")","crop (cultivo): plant grown for food or sale. Not: harvest (gathering the crop, or its season), agriculture (uncountable: the activity), livestock (animals)."],["1kr04ug","Nature: The farmers worked day and night to bring in the ______ before the rain. (starts with \"ha\")","harvest (cosecha): the gathering of crops, or the amount gathered. Not: crop (the plant grown), vintage (wine year), yield (amount produced)."],["1m43mwy","Nature: The farm keeps three hundred head of ______, mostly cows for milk. (starts with \"ca\")","cattle (ganado vacuno): cows and bulls; plural noun, no \"s\". Not: livestock (all farm animals, starts with \"li\"), herd (a group of cows), flock (sheep, birds)."],["qimfaa","Nature: A shepherd was watching his ______ of sheep on the hillside. (starts with \"fl\")","flock (rebaño): sheep, goats, birds. Not: herd (cows, elephants), pack (wolves, dogs), swarm (bees, insects)."],["b69j0n","Nature: A ______ of bees chased us across the field. (starts with \"sw\")","swarm (enjambre). Not: flock, herd, pack."],["1nvrqqq","Nature: A ______ of wolves attacked the sheep during the night. (starts with \"pa\")","pack (manada): wolves, dogs. Not: herd (cows, deer), flock (sheep, birds), school (fish)."],["15661uv","Nature: The forecast says there will be heavy ______ this afternoon, so take an umbrella. (starts with \"sh\")","showers (chubascos): short periods of rain. Not: drizzle (light fine rain), downpour (very heavy rain), storms."],["1uibyme","Nature: It isn't really raining, just a light ______. (starts with \"dr\")","drizzle (llovizna). Not: drought (sequía), shower (short, can be heavy), sleet (rain mixed with snow)."],["1nrealz","Nature: We got soaked in a sudden ______ on the way home: it rained so hard we couldn't see. (starts with \"do\")","downpour (aguacero, chaparrón). Not: drizzle, shower (weaker), flood."],["fptgco","Nature: The ______ was so thick that the airport closed: visibility was fifty metres. (starts with \"fo\")","fog (niebla): thick cloud near the ground; thinner = mist. Not: mist (starts with \"m\"), smog (pollution with fog), haze (dust or heat)."],["1o7vj8p","Nature: ______ is a mixture of rain and snow. (starts with \"sl\")","Sleet (aguanieve). Not: hail (balls of ice), snow, frost (ice on surfaces at night)."],["54qi9n","Nature: The storm brought ______ as big as golf balls, which dented cars and broke windows. (plural, starts with \"ha\")","hailstones (granizo): balls of ice; the weather itself is \"hail\" (uncountable). Not: sleet (rain and snow), snowflakes, icicles (carámbanos)."],["1vxagbb","Nature: There was a hard ______ last night, and the car windows were white with ice. (starts with \"fr\")","frost (helada, escarcha). Not: freeze (AmE \"a freeze\"), ice (general), fog."],["14waumx","Nature: Temperatures reached 44 degrees during the ______ last July. (starts with \"he\")","heatwave (ola de calor). Not: hot wave (calque), heatstroke (illness caused by heat), drought."],["8abywh","Nature: The river widens into an ______ before it meets the sea, and the tide comes in twice a day. (starts with \"es\")","estuary (estuario, ría): wide mouth of a river where it meets the tide. Not: source (where the river starts), delta (many branches), bay."],["1djjbeg","Nature: A ______ is a huge mass of ice that moves slowly down a mountain valley. (starts with \"gl\")","glacier (glaciar). Not: iceberg (floats in the sea), avalanche (sudden fall of snow), ice cap (covers a large area of land)."],["1hbyjme","Nature: Three skiers were buried when an ______ swept down the slope. (starts with \"av\")","avalanche (alud). Not: landslide (earth and rocks), glacier, blizzard (snowstorm with strong wind)."],["121xnux","Nature: Heavy rain caused a ______ that blocked the road with mud and rocks. (starts with \"la\")","landslide (corrimiento de tierras). Not: avalanche (snow), earthquake, mudslide (starts with \"m\")."],["19zvlux","Nature: Waste from the factory has ______ the river, and the fish are dying. (starts with \"co\")","contaminated (contaminado): made dirty or poisonous. Not: polluted (starts with \"p\"), contagious (disease spreading), infected (by germs)."],["1h5v8v0","Nature: Only a few hundred of these birds remain, so the species is at risk of ______. (starts with \"ex\")","extinction (extinción). Not: extermination (deliberate killing), extinguishing (putting out a fire), disappearance."],["1h4jw6z","Nature: Cutting down the rainforest destroys the natural ______ of thousands of species. (starts with \"ha\")","habitat (hábitat): natural home of an animal or plant. Not: inhabitants (people living somewhere), habitant (rare), environment (general surroundings)."],["frs1gb","Nature: Farmers ______ the seeds in spring and harvest the wheat in summer. (starts with \"so\")","sow (sembrar): sow, sowed, sown. Not: sew (coser, same sound: sew, sewed, sewn), plant (starts with \"p\"), seed."],["1sxk90t","Nature: The sunny ______ of the hills were covered with vines. (starts with \"sl\")","slopes (laderas): sides of a hill. Not: cliffs (steep rock faces, often by the sea), peaks (tops), hillsides (starts with \"h\")."],["s1w3fe","Nature: A strong ______ was blowing from the sea, so the ferries stayed in port. (starts with \"ga\")","gale (vendaval, temporal): very strong wind. Not: breeze (light wind), gust (sudden short burst), draught (cold air in a room)."],["162nid4","Nature: Close the window, there's a cold ______ in here. (BrE, starts with \"dr\")","draught (corriente de aire): BrE; AmE draft. Not: drought (sequía), breeze (outdoors, pleasant), gale."],["cmlcts","Education: She ______ from Salamanca University in 2019 with a degree in law. (starts with \"gr\")","graduated (se licenció, se graduó): \"graduate from\" a university. Not: qualified (became trained for a job: qualify as a nurse), finished, passed."],["asdace","Education: She ______ as a nurse after three years of training. (starts with \"qu\")","qualified (obtuvo el título): \"qualify as\" a professional. Not: graduated (from a university), certified, titled."],["6goivn","Education: I failed maths, so I'll have to ______ the exam in September. (BrE, starts with \"re\")","resit (volver a presentarse, recuperar): BrE; AmE retake. Not: repeat (a whole year: repeat a year), revise (study before an exam), recover (get better; false friend \"recuperar\")."],["hpie93","Education: I can't come out tonight: I have to ______ for tomorrow's exam (an American would say \"review\"). (BrE, starts with \"re\")","revise (repasar, estudiar): BrE study again before an exam; AmE review. Not: review (BrE: a critical report, or a check), resit, check."],["9rgk5u","Education: We sat a ______ exam in May to practise for the real one in June. (starts with \"mo\")","mock (simulacro): practice exam. Not: fake (not genuine, made to deceive), false, trial (test of a product, or a court case)."],["1silycl","Education: Please hand in your ______ by Friday; it should be 2,000 words long. (starts with \"as\")","assignment (trabajo, tarea): piece of work set by a teacher. Not: homework (uncountable, starts with \"h\"), task (general), subject (asignatura)."],["zepy9c","Education: My favourite ______ at school was history. (starts with \"su\")","subject (asignatura). Not: signature (firma; false friend \"asignatura\"), course (a series of lessons), matter."],["weuh23","Education: She got full ______ in the exam: 100 out of 100. (BrE, starts with \"ma\")","marks (nota, puntuación): BrE; AmE grades. Not: notes (written notes; false friend \"notas\"), points, qualifications (diplomas and certificates)."],["1msa8wx","Education: The teacher ______ the exams over the weekend and handed them back on Monday. (BrE, starts with \"ma\")","marked (corrigió): BrE; AmE graded. Not: corrected (fixed mistakes in a text), checked, noted."],["whfuoo","Education: He has a ______ in economics from the University of Valencia. (starts with \"de\")","degree (título universitario, grado). Not: career (working life; false friend \"carrera\"), title (name of a book; or Dr, Mr), grade (mark)."],["1ssqa3q","Education: She won a ______ for her excellent marks, so her university fees are paid. (starts with \"sc\")","scholarship (beca): money for study, usually for merit. Not: grant (often based on need, starts with \"g\"), scholar (person who studies), loan (repaid)."],["farf20","Education: Our ______ at the university gave a fascinating talk on Roman law. (BrE, starts with \"le\")","lecturer (profesor universitario): BrE university teacher. Not: lector (assistant language teacher, or reader in church), reader (person who reads; BrE senior academic), teacher (school)."],["1mqynk","Education: A ______ is a talk given to a large group of students at a university. (starts with \"le\")","lecture (clase magistral). Not: reading (lectura; false friend \"lectura\" = reading), conference (large meeting with many speakers), speech."],["3hlwgb","Education: I've ______ up for an evening course in Italian. (starts with \"si\")","signed (up) (me he apuntado). Not: signed in (recorded your arrival), signed off (ended), written up (written a full version)."],["1tb6bc0","Education: Students must ______ on the course before 30 September. (BrE spelling, starts with \"en\")","enrol (matricularse): BrE enrol, AmE enroll. Not: register (starts with \"r\"), inscribe (write or carve words), subscribe (to a magazine)."],["ocun97","Education: He ______ out of university after the first year to start a business. (starts with \"dr\")","dropped (out) (dejó los estudios). Not: fell out (argued), left out (excluded), gave out (handed out; or stopped working)."],["1hv4a6c","Education: She was ______ from school for fighting. (starts with \"ex\")","expelled (expulsada). Not: excluded (left out; BrE also sent away from school), evicted (from a home), exiled (from a country)."],["16ea9nj","Education: The ______ of the school is retiring after thirty years; a new one starts in September. (BrE, starts with \"he\")","headteacher (director de colegio): BrE; AmE principal. Not: director (company, film), principal (AmE; or head of a college), dean (head of a university faculty)."],["prd8w6","Education: After her degree she did a ______, a one-year postgraduate course in business. (starts with \"ma\")","master's (máster): short for \"master's degree\". Not: master (expert, or old BrE teacher), PhD (doctorate, longer), bachelor's (first degree)."],["1lv6q09","Education: In Spain, children start ______ school at six. (starts with \"pr\")","primary (primaria): AmE elementary. Not: secondary (from 12), first, nursery (before school age)."],["wkypra","Technology: My phone's ______ is almost flat; can I borrow your charger? (starts with \"ba\")","battery (batería). Not: charger (cable or plug), drums (batería musical), cell."],["67npft","Technology: Don't forget to ______ up your files in case the laptop breaks. (starts with \"ba\")","back (up) (hacer copia de seguridad). Not: save (store the current file), copy, store."],["1lfigy9","Technology: The website ______ yesterday and nobody could book tickets. (starts with \"cr\")","crashed (se cayó, se colgó): stopped working suddenly. Not: broke down (machines, cars), fell (not used), froze (stopped responding, starts with \"f\")."],["1ldrvyk","Technology: You need to ______ the app before you can use it. (starts with \"do\")","download (descargar). Not: discharge (unload; or send home from hospital), upload (send to the internet), install (starts with \"i\")."],["1guy1ip","Technology: The new software ______ is available and fixes several security problems. (starts with \"up\")","update (actualización). Not: upgrade (better version, often paid), upload, actualisation (calque, rare)."],["m53ivf","Technology: Remember to ______ the document to the email before you send it. (starts with \"at\")","attach (adjuntar). Not: attack, enclose (put in an envelope), join."],["5divso","Technology: I clicked on a ______ in the email and my computer got a virus. (starts with \"li\")","link (enlace). Not: bond (strong connection between people), chain, tie."],["wawjpw","Technology: All your messages are ______, so nobody else can read them. (starts with \"en\")","encrypted (cifrado). Not: encoded (put into code in general), hidden, coded."],["129w6gd","Technology: The ______ in the lab is so expensive that only trained staff may touch it. (starts with \"eq\")","equipment (equipo): uncountable; \"a piece of equipment\". Not: equipments (no plural), team (people), equipage."],["1he32s9","Technology: Our printer has run out of ______, so the pages come out pale. (starts with \"in\")","ink (tinta). Not: toner (powder for laser printers), paint, cartridge (container that holds the ink)."],["1eovis4","Technology: Please ______ off your phone before the film starts. (starts with \"sw\")","switch (off) (apagar). Not: switch on (encender), turn off (starts with \"t\"), close."],["fh8s8v","Technology: Can you ______ up the volume? I can't hear a thing. (starts with \"tu\")","turn (up) (subir). Not: turn down (lower), raise (no \"up\", formal), rise (no object)."],["dapqrv","Technology: The ______ control for the TV has disappeared down the side of the sofa again. (starts with \"re\")","remote (control) (mando a distancia). Not: command, controller (games console), distance control (calque)."],["1sdkdxy","Technology: He spends hours ______ the web for cheap flights. (starts with \"su\")","surfing (navegar por internet). Not: navigating (finding a route), sailing, browsing (also fits, starts with \"br\")."],["arigb","Technology: Machines have replaced workers in many factories: the whole process is now ______. (starts with \"au\")","automated (automatizado). Not: automatic (works by itself: an automatic door), autonomous (self-governing), mechanical."],["1v9vpbw","Technology: The ______ on this laptop is too small; I can hardly read the text. (starts with \"sc\")","screen (pantalla). Not: display (starts with \"d\"), monitor (separate screen of a desktop computer), keyboard."],["rp55e","Travel: Our flight was ______ by three hours because of fog. (starts with \"de\")","delayed (retrasado). Not: cancelled, postponed (moved to another date: events), late (adjective, not used with \"by\")."],["sap904","Travel: Make sure your ______ luggage fits in the overhead locker. (starts with \"ha\")","hand (luggage) (equipaje de mano): AmE carry-on. Not: handbag (bolso), hold luggage (checked in), cabin bag (starts with \"c\")."],["1268wil","Travel: We went on a day ______ to the coast and were back by dinner. (starts with \"tr\")","trip (excursión, viaje corto): going somewhere and coming back. Not: travel (uncountable activity: \"travel is expensive\"), journey (going from A to B), voyage (long sea journey)."],["1725n6m","Travel: The ______ from Madrid to Valencia takes two hours by train. (starts with \"jo\")","journey (trayecto, viaje): going from one place to another. Not: travel (uncountable), trip (short visit and back), way."],["j0huq9","Travel: The ______ across the Atlantic took eight weeks in a sailing ship. (starts with \"vo\")","voyage (travesía): long journey by sea or in space. Not: journey, travel, cruise (holiday on a ship)."],["1axty3u","Travel: We stayed in a youth ______ in the old town, sharing a room with six other travellers. (starts with \"ho\")","hostel (albergue): cheap, shared rooms. Not: hostal (Spanish small hotel), hotel, host (person who receives guests), hospice (care for the dying)."],["1enh5pc","Travel: You must show your ______ pass at the gate. (starts with \"bo\")","boarding (pass) (tarjeta de embarque). Not: embarking card (calque), ticket (the paid document), boarding card (BrE also, same first word)."],["1afog00","Travel: Please ______ in at the desk two hours before departure. (starts with \"ch\")","check (in) (facturar): check in = register at an airport or hotel. Not: invoice (factura), check out (leave a hotel), sign in."],["1dvb3fg","Travel: ______ to the museum is free on Sundays. (starts with \"ad\")","Admission (entrada): permission or price to enter. Not: entry (also fits, starts with \"e\"), entrance (the door or way in), ticket."],["s4rl2d","Travel: Book early in high ______: prices double in August. (starts with \"se\")","season (temporada alta). Not: high time (\"it's high time\" = it's late), peak (starts with \"p\"), period."],["1h6xw9h","Travel: Our hotel room had a wonderful ______ of the sea from the balcony. (starts with \"vi\")","view (vistas). Not: sight (a thing worth seeing, or the ability to see), landscape (paisaje), scenery (uncountable: natural features)."],["kymvph","Travel: We spent the afternoon seeing the ______ of Rome: the Colosseum, the Forum and St Peter's. (starts with \"si\")","sights (monumentos, lugares de interés). Not: views, scenery, sites (places where something is: a building site)."],["12bfyq9","Travel: The mountain ______ was breathtaking: lakes, forests and snowy peaks. (starts with \"sc\")","scenery (paisaje): uncountable, the natural features of an area. Not: scene (place where something happens; part of a play), sceneries (no plural), view."],["1ll3wpa","Travel: The airline lost my ______, so I had nothing to wear for three days. (starts with \"lu\")","luggage (equipaje): uncountable; \"a piece of luggage\". Not: luggages (no plural), baggage (starts with \"b\"), suitcase (countable)."],["a1rlww","Travel: We ______ a car at the airport and drove along the coast. (BrE, starts with \"hi\")","hired (alquilamos): BrE hire a car; AmE rent. Not: rented (starts with \"r\"), leased (long contract), borrowed (for free)."],["13pohuj","Travel: Excuse me, which ______ does the Seville train leave from? (starts with \"pl\")","platform (andén, vía). Not: track (AmE also used), quay (muelle), dock."],["1x68cwy","Travel: A ______ ticket is cheaper than two singles if you come back the same day. (BrE, starts with \"re\")","return (ida y vuelta): AmE round-trip. Not: round (AmE \"round-trip\"), double, back."],["1qat2bf","Travel: The flight to Tokyo has a ______ in Dubai, where we change planes. (starts with \"st\")","stopover (escala). Not: scale (balanza; false friend \"escala\"), layover (AmE, starts with \"l\"), stop."],["1mjq76","Travel: The ______ crew welcomed us aboard and showed us how to fasten our seat belts. (starts with \"ca\")","cabin (crew) (tripulación de cabina). Not: flight crew (the pilots), staff, team."],["9c6e1g","Travel: We'd like to ______ a table for four at nine o'clock. (starts with \"bo\")","book (reservar). Not: reserve (starts with \"r\"), order (food), keep."],["ops8jq","Travel: Perfume and alcohol are cheaper in the ______ shop at the airport. (starts with \"du\")","duty-free (tienda libre de impuestos). Not: tax-free (VAT refunds), free shop, customs."],["11d3ika","Travel: We had nothing to declare, so we walked straight through ______ at the airport. (starts with \"cu\")","customs (aduana): plural in this sense. Not: custom (tradition: costumbre), costume (disfraz), passport control (checks your identity)."],["die0bs","Collocations: The government has promised to ______ serious action against tax fraud. (starts with \"ta\")","take (action) (tomar medidas): \"take action against\". Not: make action, do action, put action."],["1talmdi","Collocations: Could you ______ me a favour and post this letter? (starts with \"do\")","do (a favour) (hacer un favor). Not: make a favour (calque), give, ask (ask a favour = pedir un favor)."],["6l4865","Collocations: We need to ______ a decision by Friday. (starts with \"ma\")","make (a decision) (tomar una decisión): BrE also \"take a decision\". Not: do, give, put."],["14bqn7r","Collocations: Thank you, but I'm afraid I'll have to ______ your kind invitation; I'm away that weekend. (starts with \"de\")","decline (an invitation) (rechazar cortésmente). Not: reject (blunt: plans, offers, applicants), deny (say something is untrue), refuse (less polite, starts with \"r\")."],["11atoj5","Collocations: He ______ his career to look after his children. (starts with \"sa\")","sacrificed (sacrificó): give up something valuable for something more important. Not: devoted (devote time to), abandoned, resigned."],["1q3sc2s","Collocations: She has ______ her whole life to helping refugees. (starts with \"dev\")","devoted (dedicado): \"devote time, energy or your life to + noun or -ing\". Not: dedicated (also fits, starts with \"ded\"), spent (spend time on), sacrificed."],["1j2tnvt","Collocations: I'm ______ my driving test next week and I'm so nervous. (starts with \"ta\")","taking (presentarme a): take or sit an exam. Not: passing (aprobar, not \"presentarse\"), making, giving."],["11g6qcq","Collocations: He ______ a serious mistake in the third question. (starts with \"ma\")","made (a mistake) (cometió un error). Not: did, committed (crimes; \"commit an error\" is formal), took."],["r24dif","Collocations: Don't ______ any attention to what he says; he's just jealous. (starts with \"pa\")","pay (attention) (prestar atención). Not: give, put, lend (lend an ear)."],["wgqz93","Collocations: We ______ a lot of progress in the first week. (starts with \"ma\")","made (progress) (avanzar, progresar). Not: did, got, took."],["tjef9f","Collocations: She ______ a speech at the conference about safety. (starts with \"ga\")","gave (a speech) (dio un discurso). Not: made (starts with \"m\"), said, told."],["kghig2","Collocations: All restaurants must ______ with the new hygiene rules. (starts with \"co\")","comply (cumplir): \"comply with\" a rule. Not: complete (finish), fulfil (a promise or a requirement, no \"with\"), accomplish."],["16579bv","Collocations: The president ______ his promise to cut taxes. (starts with \"ke\")","kept (a promise) (cumplió una promesa). Not: fulfilled (formal, starts with \"f\"), held, made (made a promise = prometió)."],["1iicha0","Collocations: He ______ the rules and was disqualified from the race. (starts with \"br\")","broke (the rules) (infringió las normas). Not: jumped, skipped, crossed."],["o0z9lv","Collocations: Can you ______ an eye on my bag while I go to the toilet? (starts with \"ke\")","keep (an eye on) (vigilar). Not: have, put, take."],["sw85c9","Collocations: There was ______ rain all night and the river flooded. (starts with \"he\")","heavy (rain) (lluvia fuerte); also heavy traffic, a heavy smoker. Not: strong (wind, coffee), big, hard (adverb: it rained hard)."],["cjthdt","Collocations: There's a ______ wind from the north today, so hold on to your hat. (starts with \"st\")","strong (wind) (viento fuerte). Not: heavy (rain, traffic), hard, big."],["1kplmnc","Collocations: Please be quiet, the baby is ______ asleep. (starts with \"fa\")","fast (asleep) (profundamente dormido); also \"sound asleep\". Not: deeply, hard, strongly."],["1fn7y30","Collocations: I am ______ aware of the risks, thank you. (starts with \"fu\")","fully (aware) (plenamente consciente). Not: highly, deeply, strongly."],["wa1q23","Collocations: It is ______ unlikely that the flight will leave on time. (starts with \"hi\")","highly (unlikely) (muy improbable). Not: deeply, strongly, heavily."],["1vzjq0c","Collocations: I'm ______ grateful for all your help. (starts with \"dee\")","deeply (grateful) (profundamente agradecido). Not: highly, strongly, fully."],["2ajjpa","Collocations: Smoking is ______ prohibited anywhere in this building. (starts with \"st\")","strictly (prohibited) (terminantemente prohibido). Not: strongly (recommend, oppose), highly, heavily."],["1crv8xd","Collocations: We ______ advise passengers to arrive two hours before departure. (starts with \"st\")","strongly (advise) (recomendamos encarecidamente). Not: strictly (prohibited, forbidden), highly (recommend, starts with \"h\"), deeply."],["wk0j9x","Collocations: The two versions of the story are ______ different: they hardly agree on anything. (starts with \"va\")","vastly (different) (enormemente distintas). Not: hugely (starts with \"h\"), heavily, strongly."],["kpsxjx","Collocations: The job requires a ______ knowledge of the regulations. (starts with \"th\")","thorough (knowledge) (conocimiento profundo, exhaustivo). Not: through (a través), thoughtful (considerate), deep (starts with \"d\")."],["apuawj","Collocations: Can you give me a ______ estimate of the cost? It doesn't have to be exact. (starts with \"ro\")","rough (estimate) (cálculo aproximado). Not: approximate (starts with \"ap\"), raw (uncooked), hard."],["vikkeg","Collocations: There's only a ______ chance of rain, so I'll leave the umbrella at home. (starts with \"sl\")","slight (chance) (ligera probabilidad). Not: small (starts with \"sm\"), light, thin."],["y37z1f","Collocations: The company is in ______ financial difficulties and may have to close. (starts with \"se\")","serious (difficulties) (graves dificultades). Not: grave (formal, starts with \"g\"), heavy, hard."],["1vzb2xb","Collocations: The firm ______ a profit of two million euros last year. (starts with \"ma\")","made (a profit) (obtuvo beneficios). Not: won (money in a game), gained, earned (money for work)."],["su60s8","Collocations: Could you ______ me a hand with these boxes? They're heavy. (starts with \"le\")","lend (a hand) (echar una mano); also \"give me a hand\". Not: borrow, throw, take."],["1g5zleu","Collocations: The minister ______ the blame for the delays and resigned. (starts with \"to\")","took (the blame) (asumió la culpa). Not: got, carried, accepted (formal, starts with \"a\")."],["jzk1nx","Collocations: Let's ______ the matter at the next meeting. (starts with \"di\")","discuss (tratar, hablar de): no preposition after it. Not: discuss about (wrong), argue (disagree angrily), dispute."],["3ls472","Collocations: She ______ an important role in the negotiations. (starts with \"pl\")","played (a role) (desempeñó un papel). Not: did, made, had (starts with \"h\")."],["1tc5d76","Collocations: The new rules will ______ effect next month. (starts with \"ta\")","take (effect) (entrar en vigor); also \"come into effect\". Not: make, have, give."],["1fx72ji","Collocations: I'm afraid we can't ______ a new car right now. (starts with \"af\")","afford (permitirse): have enough money for. Not: allow (give permission), support, permit."],["1s3y5a","Collocations: You should ______ advantage of the sales and buy a new coat. (starts with \"ta\")","take (advantage of) (aprovechar). Not: make, get, have."],["10r75q7","Collocations: Doctors advise patients with high blood pressure to ______ salty food. (starts with \"av\")","avoid (evitar): keep away from; \"avoid + noun or -ing\". Not: prevent (stop something happening), escape (get away from), refuse."],["14thipl","Collocations: Seat belts ______ thousands of deaths every year. (starts with \"pr\")","prevent (evitar, impedir): stop something happening; \"prevent someone from doing\". Not: avoid (keep away from), protect (keep safe: protect people from), anticipate (expect; Spanish \"prevenir\" can mean warn)."],["1pp1j2f","Collocations: The minister ______ that he had received the money. (starts with \"de\")","denied (negó): said something is not true; \"deny + -ing or that\". Not: refused (said no to doing), declined, rejected."],["r0j1rd","Collocations: The board ______ the proposal because it was too expensive. (starts with \"rej\")","rejected (rechazó): did not accept a plan, offer or person. Not: declined (polite: invitations, offers), denied (said not true), refused (+ to-infinitive)."],["1n44pue","Collocations: He ______ to help us, even though we asked politely. (starts with \"ref\")","refused (se negó): \"refuse + to-infinitive\". Not: denied (+ -ing or that), rejected (+ noun), declined (also fits, starts with \"d\")."],["1dkpiyo","Collocations: Her face ______ a bell, but I can't remember her name. (starts with \"ri\")","rings (a bell) (me suena). Not: sounds (false friend \"suena\"), calls, plays."],["1daml3y","Collocations: I need to ______ some money from the cash machine. (starts with \"wi\")","withdraw (sacar dinero). Not: take out (two words), remove, extract."],["1nes9nm","Collocations: Could you ______ me 20 euros until Friday? (starts with \"le\")","lend (prestar): give for a time. Not: borrow (take for a time: can I borrow 20 euros?), loan (noun; AmE verb), owe (deber)."],["gdqlxg","Collocations: Can I ______ your pen for a moment? (starts with \"bo\")","borrow (pedir prestado, tomar prestado): take for a time. Not: lend (give for a time), loan, rent."],["3e0bt0","Collocations: You know what they ______: better late than never. (starts with \"sa\")","say (dicen): \"you know what they say\" introduces a saying. Not: tell (needs a person: tell me), speak (a language), state (formal)."],["1tpc572","Collocations: The cathedral has been under ______ for over a century. (starts with \"co\")","construction (en construcción): \"under construction\". Not: building (in construction, calque), works, repair (under repair, starts with \"r\")."],["kni2jy","Collocations: You can stay in our spare room for the time ______, until you find a flat. (starts with \"be\")","being (por ahora): \"for the time being\" = for now. Not: going, doing, making."],["sbwihf","Collocations: She has been ______ about the new rules from the start: she thinks they won't work. (starts with \"sce\")","sceptical (escéptica): doubting; AmE skeptical. Not: cynical (believes people act only from self-interest), critical (starts with \"cr\"), suspicious (thinks something is wrong)."],["6x96fc","Prepositions: The judge sentenced him ______ six years in prison. (one word)","to: \"sentence someone to\" a punishment. Not: for (the crime: sentenced for theft), with, at."],["13101az","Prepositions: Mark is completely dedicated ______ his family. (one word)","to: \"dedicated to\" (and devoted to). Not: with, for, in."],["1asbdvd","Prepositions: He was accused ______ stealing from his employer. (one word)","of: \"accuse someone of + -ing\". Not: for (blame for, charge with), about, with."],["kw7r6x","Prepositions: He was charged ______ murder and will stand trial in May. (one word)","with: \"charge someone with\" a crime. Not: of (accuse of), for, about."],["18y3mdx","Prepositions: They blamed the driver ______ the accident. (one word)","for: \"blame a person for a thing\". Compare: they blamed the accident ON the driver. Not: of, about, with."],["1cdj2td","Prepositions: They blamed the accident ______ the driver. (one word)","on: \"blame a thing on a person\". Compare: they blamed the driver FOR the accident. Not: to, of, at."],["3zu9ws","Prepositions: It's time you faced up ______ the facts: the business has failed. (one word)","to: \"face up to\" = accept something unpleasant. Not: on, with, at."],["15oaq4a","Prepositions: The night supervisor is ______ charge of the whole team. (one word)","in: \"in charge of\" = responsible for. Not: on, at, under."],["dlmkly","Prepositions: Whether we go or not depends ______ the weather. (one word)","on: \"depend on\". Not: of (calque \"depender de\"), from, in."],["1utm64q","Prepositions: I've never been very good ______ maths. (one word)","at: \"good at\" a subject or activity. Not: in (calque \"bueno en\"), on, with."],["14su8tg","Prepositions: My sister is married ______ a pilot. (one word)","to: \"married to\". Not: with (calque \"casada con\"), by, at."],["w2psae","Prepositions: He apologised ______ being late. (one word)","for: \"apologise (to someone) for + -ing\". Not: of, about, by."],["fz5f59","Prepositions: The film is based ______ a true story. (one word)","on: \"based on\". Not: in (calque \"basada en\"), of, at."],["azmaxx","Prepositions: She insisted ______ paying for dinner. (one word)","on: \"insist on + -ing\". Not: in (calque \"insistir en\"), to, about."],["1ssngv7","Prepositions: I'm really looking forward ______ seeing you again. (one word)","to: \"look forward to + -ing\" (to is a preposition here). Not: for, on, at."],["qtfuvb","Prepositions: He finally succeeded ______ passing the exam at the third attempt. (one word)","in: \"succeed in + -ing\". Not: to, on, at."],["q61tq9","Prepositions: The flat consists ______ three bedrooms, a kitchen and a bathroom. (one word)","of: \"consist of\" = be made up of. Not: in (calque \"consistir en\"; \"consist in\" = have as its essence, formal), on, from."],["1023edu","Prepositions: We arrived ______ Madrid at noon. (one word)","in: \"arrive in\" a city or country. Not: to (calque \"llegar a\"), at (a building or small place: arrive at the airport)."],["1bld87j","Prepositions: We arrived ______ the airport two hours before the flight. (one word)","at: \"arrive at\" a building or a point. Not: to (calque), in (cities, countries)."],["1smgc4q","Prepositions: Valencia is famous ______ its paella and its oranges. (one word)","for: \"famous for\". Not: by, of, with."],["1jr6p00","Prepositions: There has been a sharp rise ______ house prices this year. (one word)","in: \"a rise in\" something = increase in its amount. Not: of (\"the rise of China\" = growing power), on, at."],["1cb2x3r","Prepositions: Prices rose ______ 5 % last year, from 100 to 105 euros. (one word)","by: \"rise or fall by\" = the size of the change; \"rise to\" = the final level. Not: in, of, at."],["1ftp9mc","Prepositions: The minister was criticised ______ the way he handled the crisis. (one word)","for: \"criticise someone for\". Not: by (the person who criticises), of, about."],["9ljad6","Prepositions: The captain is responsible ______ the safety of everyone on board. (one word)","for: \"responsible for\". Not: of (calque \"responsable de\"), about, with."],["bsx558","Prepositions: She's very interested ______ learning to fly. (one word)","in: \"interested in + noun or -ing\". Not: on, for, about."],["kovm7g","Prepositions: She is perfectly capable ______ running the company on her own. (one word)","of: \"capable of + -ing\"; compare \"able to + infinitive\". Not: to, for, in."],["h3g7xn","Prepositions: Are you aware ______ the risks of this treatment? (one word)","of: \"aware of\". Not: about, on, with."],["220vx5","Prepositions: He graduated ______ Oxford with a degree in history. (one word)","from: \"graduate from\" a university; \"graduate in\" a subject. Not: of, at (AmE sometimes), on."],["z2s319","Prepositions: My little brother is afraid ______ the dark. (one word)","of: \"afraid of\". Not: to (calque \"miedo a\"), from, about."],["1eealhn","Prepositions: Don't worry ______ the exam; you've studied hard. (one word)","about: \"worry about\". Not: for (worry for someone's safety, less common), of, on."],["1jsh13m","Inversion: (a) No sooner had the plane landed ______ the passengers stood up. (b) Hardly had the plane landed ______ the passengers stood up. (one word each)","(a) than (b) when. No sooner ... than; Hardly / Scarcely / Barely ... when; both with had + subject + past participle. Not: then, that."],["7vurlb","Inversion: Same meaning as \"I have never seen such a long queue\": Never ______ such a long queue. (three words)","have I seen. Negative adverb first, then auxiliary + subject + main verb. Not: I have seen (no inversion), seen I have."],["p4m19c","Inversion: Not until the last aircraft had landed ______ home. (three words; subject \"she\", verb \"go\")","did she go. Not until + clause, then the inversion in the MAIN clause, never in the until-clause. Not: she went, went she."],["xg36bm","Inversion: ______ told about the road closure, we would have taken another route. (three words; = If we had been)","Had we been. Inverted third conditional: drop \"if\" and put \"had\" first. Not: Did we, If had we, Were we been."],["18n8wiv","Inversion: ______ you need any help, just call reception. (one word; formal = If you need)","Should. Inverted first conditional, formal. Not: Would, Had, Were."],["ewrxrn","Inversion: ______ I in your position, I would accept the offer. (one word; = If I were)","Were. Inverted second conditional, formal. Not: Was (not inverted in this pattern), Had, Should."],["1nzsnpq","Inversion: Not only ______ she write the songs, but she also produces the albums. (one word)","does. Not only + auxiliary + subject; the \"but ... also\" part has normal order. Not: she does, is."],["brlr2o","Inversion: Only after the investigation ______ the truth come out. (one word)","did. Only after / Only when / Only then: inversion in the main clause. Not: the truth did, has."],["h5ya7u","Inversion: Under no circumstances ______ you leave the building during the drill. (one word, starts with \"sh\")","should (also \"must\", \"may\"). Under no circumstances / On no account + auxiliary + subject. Not: you should (no inversion)."],["rbg7rl","Inversion: Little ______ he know that the police were watching him. (one word)","did. \"Little did he know\" = he had no idea. Not: he knew, does."],["1zgpj5","Inversion: So bad ______ the weather that the flight was cancelled. (one word)","was. So + adjective + be + subject + that. Not: the weather was, did."],["1ig1dov","Inversion: Rarely ______ we seen such a storm on this coast. (one word, present perfect)","have. Rarely / Seldom + auxiliary + subject. Not: we have, did."],["1evvm5n","Inversion: Barely ______ we sat down when the fire alarm went off. (one word)","had. Barely / Hardly / Scarcely + had + subject + past participle ... when. Not: did (needs \"sit\"), have."],["bsy9na","Inversion: At no time ______ the pilot aware of the danger. (one word)","was. At no time + auxiliary or be + subject. Not: the pilot was, did."],["l4w9xs","Inversion: Seldom ______ he eat breakfast before work: he's always in a hurry. (one word, present simple)","does. Seldom + do/does + subject + base verb. Not: he does, is."],["1cyksc6","Inversion: Only then ______ I realise how serious the mistake was. (one word)","did. Only then + auxiliary + subject + base verb. Not: I did, I realised."],["htuukh","Possessive: I'm spending the weekend at my ______. (possessive of \"aunt\")","aunt's (en casa de mi tía): 's with the noun \"house\" left out. Not: aunt, aunts', the house of my aunt (correct but not one word)."],["1cdavkl","Possessive: I bought this bread at the ______ on the corner. (possessive of \"baker\")","baker's (panadería): shops and offices named after the person: the baker's, the butcher's, the chemist's, the travel agent's. Not: baker, bakers."],["90dw2y","Possessive: I have an appointment at the ______ at four. (possessive of \"dentist\")","dentist's: \"at the dentist's\", \"at the hairdresser's\" (surgery or shop left out). Not: dentists', dentists."],["gwnnyr","Possessive: The ______ toys were all over the floor. (possessive of \"children\")","children's: irregular plural without s takes 's. Not: childrens', childrens's, children'."],["1wuh98n","Possessive: The ______ canteen is on the ground floor; all the staff eat there. (possessive of \"employees\")","employees': regular plural ending in s takes only an apostrophe. Not: employees's, employee's (one employee), employees."],["128vr4c","Possessive: Have you read ______ newspaper? (possessive of \"yesterday\")","yesterday's: time words take 's (today's news, next week's meeting). Not: yesterday, the yesterday's."],["16k8jrv","Possessive: After a ______ holiday I felt much better. (possessive of \"week\")","week's: a week's holiday, a day's work. Not: week, weeks', weeks."],["in6bb8","Possessive: You must give your employer four ______ notice before you leave. (possessive of \"weeks\")","weeks': plural time noun: two weeks' notice, three years' experience. Not: week's, weeks, weeks's."],["mna8hj","Possessive: This car isn't mine, it's my ______. (possessive of \"parents\")","parents': two parents, so the apostrophe goes after the s; the noun \"car\" is left out. Not: parent's (one parent), parents's."],["1d8fbba","Possessive: Ana and ______ flat is near the beach; they bought it together. (possessive of \"Pedro\")","Pedro's: shared ownership = 's only on the last name (Ana and Pedro's flat). Separate ownership: Ana's and Pedro's flats. Not: Ana's and Pedro's (two flats), Pedros'."],["fgesx3","Possessive: The man next ______ dog barks all night. (possessive of \"door\")","door's: the 's goes at the end of the whole noun group (the man next door's dog). Not: the man's next door dog."],["11hvvbc","Possessive: Is this umbrella ______? (possessive pronoun of \"you\")","yours: possessive pronouns never take an apostrophe (yours, hers, ours, theirs, its). Not: your's, yours'."],["130lhb0","Possessive: The company changed ______ logo last year. (possessive of \"it\")","its: no apostrophe; it's = it is or it has. Not: it's, its'."],["1lg716q","Possessive: Whenever she goes to Italy, she stays at her ______ villa in Tuscany. (possessive of \"grandmother\")","grandmother's: one owner, so 's. Not: grandmothers' (several grandmothers), grandmothers, grandmother."],["1ugd5xb","Possessive: The ______ changing room is on the left. (possessive of \"women\")","women's: irregular plural + 's. Not: womens', woman's (one woman), womens."],["vkeo81","Verb pairs: Unemployment has ______ for the third month in a row. (rise or raise?)","risen: rise, rose, risen = go up, no object. Not: raised (needs an object), rose (past simple), rised."],["z9p2ew","Verb pairs: The airline has ______ its fares by 10 %. (rise or raise?)","raised: raise, raised, raised + object (raise prices, raise your hand). Not: risen (no object), rose."],["hk8e87","Verb pairs: The sun ______ at six this morning. (rise or raise? past simple)","rose: rise, rose, risen. Not: raised (needs an object), risen (participle), rised."],["notb74","Verb pairs: If you have a question, please ______ your hand. (rise or raise?)","raise: + object. Not: rise (no object)."],["h9mc0g","Verb pairs: She has ______ three children on her own. (rise or raise?)","raised: raise children = bring them up. Not: risen, rose (no object)."],["1babkqw","Verb pairs: I'm going to ______ down for an hour; I've got a headache. (lie or lay?)","lie: lie, lay, lain, lying = be horizontal, no object. Not: lay (needs an object)."],["32zry4","Verb pairs: Yesterday I ______ in bed until noon. (lie = be horizontal; past simple)","lay: the past of lie is lay. Not: laid (past of lay + object), lied (told lies), lain (participle)."],["1frf8v0","Verb pairs: The hen has ______ three eggs this week. (lie or lay?)","laid: lay, laid, laid + object. Not: lain (lie), lied, layed."],["oaejr3","Verb pairs: He ______ the baby gently in the cot. (lie or lay? past simple)","laid: put down carefully + object. Not: lay (past of lie, no object), lied."],["180pwpi","Verb pairs: The suspect ______ to the police about where he had been. (lie = say something untrue; past simple)","lied: lie, lied, lied (tell lies) is regular. Not: lay, laid, lain."],["1pfraga","Verb pairs: Your keys are ______ on the kitchen table. (lie or lay? -ing form)","lying: -ing form of lie (be horizontal); laying = putting down. Not: laying, lieing."],["md1xht","Verb pairs: ______ the map flat on the table so we can all see it. (lie or lay? imperative)","Lay: + object. Not: Lie (no object)."],["k380nm","Verb pairs: The town ______ at the foot of the mountains. (lie or lay? present simple)","lies: lie = be in a place. Not: lays (needs an object), laid."],["i1xruk","Verb pairs: A problem has ______ with the booking system. (arise or arouse?)","arisen: arise, arose, arisen = appear, happen (problems, questions), no object. Not: aroused (needs an object), arised, arose (past simple)."],["1oo1sz2","Verb pairs: His strange behaviour ______ the suspicion of the police. (arise or arouse? past simple)","aroused: arouse + object (arouse suspicion, interest). Not: arose (no object), arisen."],["1g8xqkt","Verb pairs: The workers ______ three trees to make room for the road. (fall or fell? past simple)","felled: fell, felled, felled = cut down a tree. Not: fell (past of fall), fallen."],["1x61un9","Verb pairs: An old tree ______ across the road during the storm. (fall or fell? past simple)","fell: fall, fell, fallen. Not: felled (cut down by someone), falled."],["11v9zfh","Causative: I had my car ______ at the garage yesterday. (repair)","repaired: have + object + past participle = someone else did it for you. Not: repair, repairing, to repair."],["6bcm9g","Causative: He ______ his phone stolen at the hotel pool. (one word, past, starts with \"h\")","had: \"have something done\" also = something bad happened to you. Not: was, did, made."],["qrebos","Causative: Within minutes the comedian had the whole audience ______. (laugh)","laughing: have + object + -ing = cause an action that goes on. Not: laughed, to laugh."],["1r3ux6o","Causative: I'll have the porter ______ your bags up to the room. (bring)","bring: have + person + base form = ask someone to do something. Not: to bring, brought, bringing."],["7a1c2x","Causative: I finally got my brother ______ me move the sofa. (help; two words)","to help: get + person + to-infinitive (persuade). Not: help (that is \"have someone help\"), helping, helped."],["rif1w4","Causative: We're ______ the kitchen painted next week. (have)","having: present continuous for an arrangement + causative. Not: have, had, getting the kitchen paint."],["1nzz18f","Causative: You should get your eyes ______ before you renew your licence. (test)","tested: get + object + past participle = have something done (more informal). Not: test, testing, to test."],["vgjie1","Causative: What is the difference? (a) I cut my hair. (b) I had my hair cut.","(a) You cut it yourself. (b) A hairdresser cut it for you: have + object + past participle."],["vkjyot","Causative: The teacher made us ______ the essay. (rewrite)","rewrite: make + object + base form. Passive: we were made to rewrite it. Not: to rewrite (only in the passive), rewriting, rewritten."],["1mfxifk","Causative: We were made ______ for two hours at the border. (wait; two words)","to wait: the passive of make takes the to-infinitive. Not: wait, waiting, waited."],["1q87jr4","Causative: My parents let me ______ out until midnight. (stay)","stay: let + object + base form. \"Let\" has no passive: say \"I was allowed to stay\". Not: to stay, staying."],["1iquyci","Causative: When I was sixteen I was ______ to stay out until midnight. (allow)","allowed: the passive form for \"let\" (let has no passive). Not: let, letted, permitted to (formal, also possible)."],["1tcnn68","So/neither: \"I love jazz.\" Answer: \"______ do I.\" (one word)","So: agreeing with a positive statement: So + auxiliary + subject. Not: Neither (negative statements), Too (Me too / I do too)."],["1am6a2o","So/neither: \"I don't eat meat.\" Answer: \"______ do I.\" (one word, starts with \"Ne\")","Neither (also \"Nor do I\"; informal \"Me neither\"). Not: So do I (positive statements), Either do I."],["drkczj","So/neither: \"We were at the concert last week.\" Answer: \"So ______ I!\" (one word)","was: the auxiliary matches the tense and verb of the first statement (were → was for \"I\"). Not: did, am, were."],["1hewo7i","So/neither: \"I've never been to Japan.\" Answer: \"Neither ______ I.\" (one word)","have: \"never\" makes the statement negative, so neither; present perfect → have. Not: do, did, am."],["1h81nj","So/neither: \"She can't swim.\" Answer: \"Nor ______ her brother.\" (one word)","can: modal verb repeated. Not: does, can't (no double negative after nor), is."],["1n3b4lu","So/neither: \"I'd love a coffee.\" Answer: \"So ______ I.\" (one word)","would: I'd = I would. Not: had, do, am."],["1iih6h1","So/neither: \"Tom passed the exam.\" Answer: \"So ______ Laura.\" (one word)","did: past simple → did. Not: was, has, passed."],["5ieswa","So/neither: \"I'm not tired.\" You disagree: \"I ______.\" (one word)","am: to disagree, give a short answer with the opposite auxiliary; no so or neither. Not: So am I (agrees with a positive), Neither am I (agrees), I'm (no contraction at the end)."],["10kjk11","So/neither: \"I love this film.\" You disagree: \"I ______.\" (one word)","don't: short answer with the opposite auxiliary. Not: So do I (agrees), Neither do I, not."],["pttx2d","So/neither: \"I didn't like the hotel.\" Answer: \"______ did my wife.\" (one word, starts with \"No\")","Nor (= Neither did my wife). Not: So (positive), Either, Not."],["wtm1ak","So/neither: \"I don't like coffee.\" Informal answer: \"Me ______.\" (one word)","neither: \"Me neither\" agrees with a negative; \"Me too\" only with a positive. Not: too, so, either (AmE informal \"Me either\", avoid in exams)."],["wpzt69","So/neither: \"He has finished his report.\" Answer: \"So ______ she.\" (one word)","has: present perfect → has. Not: does, did, is."],["1trou1u","Verb patterns: After such a brave performance, the players didn't deserve ______ so harshly by the press. (criticise; three words)","to be criticised: deserve + to-infinitive, here passive. Not: be criticised, being criticised, to being criticised."],["1rxx12y","Verb patterns: They accused him ______ in the exam. (cheat; two words)","of cheating: accuse someone of + -ing. Not: to cheat, cheating, that he cheats."],["qqyp8c","Verb patterns: Profits ______ to fall next year. (expect; two words)","are expected: passive reporting verb + to-infinitive (are expected / thought / believed to). Not: expect to fall, are expecting, are expected falling."],["1sjypo3","Verb patterns: He is said ______ the richest man in town. (be; two words)","to be: passive reporting verb + to-infinitive. Not: being, that he is (needs \"It is said that\"), be."],["1otamxu","Verb patterns: She is believed ______ the country last week. (leave; three words)","to have left: perfect infinitive for an action before the time of believing. Not: to leave, to be left, leaving."],["t0orc","Verb patterns: (a) I stopped ______ last year. (smoke) (b) On the way home I stopped ______ some bread. (buy)","(a) smoking: stop + -ing = give up the activity. (b) to buy: stop + to-infinitive = stop in order to do something else."],["o74c2r","Verb patterns: (a) Remember ______ the door when you leave. (lock) (b) I clearly remember ______ the door. (lock)","(a) to lock: remember + to-infinitive = don't forget a duty. (b) locking: remember + -ing = have a memory of a past action."],["shqh33","Verb patterns: (a) I'll never forget ______ the Grand Canyon. (see) (b) Don't forget ______ the letter. (post)","(a) seeing: forget + -ing = a past experience. (b) to post: forget + to-infinitive = a duty."],["ajl11i","Verb patterns: (a) We regret ______ you that your application was unsuccessful. (inform) (b) I regret ______ her the secret. (tell)","(a) to inform: regret + to-infinitive = formal bad news now. (b) telling: regret + -ing = sorry about something you did."],["1vooor0","Verb patterns: (a) If it won't start, try ______ it off and on again. (switch) (b) I tried ______ the box, but it was too heavy. (lift)","(a) switching: try + -ing = do something as an experiment. (b) to lift: try + to-infinitive = make an effort."],["fcyaxy","Verb patterns: (a) He went on ______ for two hours without a break. (talk) (b) After the introduction, she went on ______ the results. (explain)","(a) talking: go on + -ing = continue the same thing. (b) to explain: go on + to-infinitive = move on to something new."],["5rwmjk","Verb patterns: Would you mind ______ the window? (open)","opening: mind + -ing. Not: to open, open."],["1n525qa","Verb patterns: She suggested ______ to the cinema. (go)","going: suggest + -ing, or suggest that we (should) go. Not: to go, us to go."],["xv4wdy","Verb patterns: He finally admitted ______ the money. (take)","taking (also \"having taken\"): admit + -ing. Not: to take, take."],["t5cmjv","Verb patterns: Despite the strike, they managed ______ the project on time. (finish; two words)","to finish: manage + to-infinitive. Not: finishing, finish."],["1si31lk","Verb patterns: (a) I'm used to ______ up early. (get) (b) I used to ______ up early, but now I sleep in. (get)","(a) getting: be used to + -ing = be accustomed. (b) get: used to + base form = a past habit."],["spag2","Verb patterns: Despite ______ tired, she finished the report. (be)","being: despite + noun or -ing. Not: despite of, despite she was (use \"although she was\")."],["1m2nzp2","Verb patterns: The doctor advised me ______ for a week. (rest; two words)","to rest: advise + object + to-infinitive; with no object, advise + -ing (he advised resting). Not: resting (after an object), rest."],["zi1vdk","Verb patterns: It's no use ______; they won't change anything. (complain)","complaining: it's no use / it's no good + -ing. Not: to complain, complain."],["wknxdy","Verb patterns: She's considering ______ to Barcelona. (move)","moving: consider + -ing. Not: to move, move."],["13nal2a","Verb patterns: He denied ______ the window. (break)","breaking: deny + -ing (or deny that). Not: to break, break."],["96ie15","Verb patterns: There's no point ______; the last bus has gone. (wait; two words)","in waiting: there's no point in + -ing. Not: to wait, waiting (without \"in\" is informal), for waiting."],["1qq9o02","Verb patterns: (a) I'd rather ______ at home tonight. (stay) (b) I'd rather you ______ in here. (not smoke; two words)","(a) stay: would rather + base form. (b) didn't smoke: would rather + another subject + past simple. Not: to stay, don't smoke."],["1iocakm","Verb patterns: It's high time we ______; the last train goes in ten minutes. (leave)","left: it's (high) time + subject + past simple. Not: leave, will leave, have left."],["u0qpa4","Verb patterns: I can't afford ______ a new car this year. (buy; two words)","to buy: afford + to-infinitive. Not: buying, buy."],["3491j2","Verb patterns: She carefully avoided ______ the question. (answer)","answering: avoid + -ing. Not: to answer, answer."]]);
